{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Un94HPwA6qvfrAGcXNTo1m","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Experiment Plan — policy_ambiguity_safety\n2\t# Post-MVP, targeting EMNLP 2026 (ARR Aug cycle)\n3\t# Claims reference paper_framing.md\n4\t\n5\texperiments:\n6\t  # === P0: Must-run for paper ===\n7\t\n8\t  - id: plan_001\n9\t    name: full_study_clause_generation\n10\t    claim: \"C1, C2, C3\"\n11\t    description: >\n12\t      Generate remaining clauses for full study: coreferential (50 new),\n13\t      authorization_scope (50 new), lexical (+20 to reach 50),\n14\t      incompleteness (+20 to reach 50). Total 140 new clauses.\n15\t      Validate all 300 clauses (50/type × 6 types) for completeness\n16\t      and cross-type balance. Mix CP format per Reviewer suggestion\n17\t      (labeled + unlabeled).\n18\t    priority: P0\n19\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n20\t    deps: []\n21\t    status: planned\n22\t\n23\t  - id: plan_001b\n24\t    name: new_type_mini_pilot\n25\t    claim: \"C1 (validation)\"\n26\t    description: >\n27\t      Mini-pilot for coreferential + authorization_scope (never tested):\n28\t      5 clauses/type × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes.\n29\t      Verify: (a) ambiguous triggers violations (b) unambiguous control < 15%.\n30\t      If systematic issues found, fix clause design before full study.\n31\t      API cost negligible (~$2). Per Reviewer warning on untested types.\n32\t    priority: P0\n33\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n34\t    deps: [plan_001]\n35\t    status: planned\n36\t\n37\t  - id: plan_002\n38\t    name: full_study_api\n39\t    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4, C5\"\n40\t    description: >\n41\t      Run 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1,\n42\t      claude-sonnet-4-6) = 1,800 episodes on τ²-bench. Cross-judge\n43\t      evaluation. Output: episodes.jsonl + judgments.jsonl. No GPU needed.\n44\t      Claude via OpenRouter proxy (base_url=http://47.94.22.126/v1).\n45\t      [2026-05-20] Claude added per distill gap (4/8 papers use Claude baseline).\n46\t    priority: P0\n47\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n48\t    deps: [plan_001, plan_001b, plan_010]\n49\t    status: planned\n50\t\n51\t  - id: plan_003\n52\t    name: full_study_local\n53\t    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4, C5\"\n54\t    description: >\n55\t      Run 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B,\n56\t      Qwen3-32B-AWQ via vLLM) = 1,200 episodes on τ²-bench.\n57\t      Requires 1× RTX PRO 6000 (48GB). Cross-judge uses API models.\n58\t      Can run in parallel with plan_002.\n59\t    priority: P0\n60\t    gpu_budget_hours: 48\n61\t    deps: [plan_001]\n62\t    status: planned\n63\t\n64\t  - id: plan_004\n65\t    name: full_study_analysis\n66\t    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4\"\n67\t    description: >\n68\t      Statistical analysis of full study data (3,000 episodes):\n69\t      (a) Binary effect per type with bootstrap CI (C1)\n70\t      (b) Omnibus χ² + pairwise across 6 types (C2)\n71\t      (c) Visibility comparison: CP vs scopal rates (C3)\n72\t      (d) Model × type interaction: 5×6 contingency + logistic regression (C4)\n73\t      Report effect sizes + CI for all comparisons per Reviewer suggestion.\n74\t      [Dream A3] Power analysis: report MDE for C2 (given N=250/type pooled)\n75\t      and C3 (given N=250 per type). If V < 0.20 but MDE > observed V,\n76\t      discuss underpowered possibility.\n77\t      [Dream A4] TOST equivalence test with both ±15pp and ±10pp margins.\n78\t      Justify margin choice explicitly.\n79\t      [Dream A10] Report per-type information delta (token count difference\n80\t      between ambiguous and unambiguous variants) as control variable.\n81\t      [Dream B&K] Inter-model agreement on ambiguous clauses: do 5 models\n82\t      adopt same or different interpretations? (supplementary analysis)\n83\t    priority: P0\n84\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n85\t    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n86\t    status: planned\n87\t\n88\t  - id: plan_005\n89\t    name: error_analysis\n90\t    claim: \"C5\"\n91\t    description: >\n92\t      Qualitative analysis of agent traces from full study:\n93\t      (a) Sample 50 violation traces per type (300 total)\n94\t      (b) Classify failure modes (scope misapplication, conservative refusal,\n95\t          assumption-based action, arbitrary rule selection, etc.)\n96\t      (c) Cross-type failure mode distribution\n97\t      (d) Visibility mechanism: compare CP traces (explicit conflict detection\n98\t          behavior) vs scopal traces (surface scope adoption without awareness)\n99\t      (e) Model-specific failure patterns (connect to C4)\n100\t    priority: P0\n101\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n102\t    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n103\t    status: planned\n104\t\n105\t  # === P1: Important for robustness ===\n106\t\n107\t  - id: plan_006\n108\t    name: reliability_test\n109\t    claim: \"C1, C2\"\n110\t    description: >\n111\t      Test-retest reliability: select 30 representative clauses (5/type),\n112\t      run 3 independent replicates × 2 conditions × 5 models = 900 episodes.\n113\t      Compute ICC for per-clause violation rates. Addresses Reviewer warning\n114\t      about ±8pp sampling noise (scopal 51.7% → 43.3% across MVP/diag).\n115\t      Bootstrap CI width should be < 10pp for key comparisons.\n116\t    priority: P1\n117\t    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n118\t    deps: [plan_001]\n119\t    status: planned\n120\t\n121\t  - id: plan_007\n122\t    name: realism_validation\n123\t    claim: \"C1 (methodological)\"\n124\t    description: >\n125\t      Validate synthetic ambiguity injection realism:\n126\t      (a) Linguistic property comparison with DRIP-R natural ambiguities\n127\t          (sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR) + KS tests\n128\t      (b) Optional: discriminator test if DRIP-R data accessible\n129\t      Addresses RC4 (ecological validity).\n130\t    priority: P1\n131\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n132\t    deps: [plan_001]\n133\t    status: planned\n134\t\n135\t  - id: plan_009\n136\t    name: judge_calibration\n137\t    claim: \"C1 (methodological)\"\n138\t    description: >\n139\t      LLM-as-judge calibration per distilled research norm (5/8 papers):\n140\t      (a) Sample 100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition\n141\t      (b) Human expert labels (2 annotators, target κ ≥ 0.75)\n142\t      (c) Compute judge precision/recall/F1 against human ground truth\n143\t      (d) Per-severity-tier agreement rates\n144\t      (e) Report in Method section as standard practice per AgentAuditor/DRIP-R\n145\t      [Dream A7] Upgraded P1→P0: Dream best-tier reviewers identified this\n146\t      as \"single most critical missing validation.\" Without it, entire\n147\t      measurement chain from episode to violation label is unvalidated.\n148\t      κ=0.91 measures LLM-LLM agreement, not accuracy.\n149\t    priority: P0\n150\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n151\t    deps: [plan_002]\n152\t    status: planned\n153\t\n154\t  - id: plan_010\n155\t    name: perturbation_control\n156\t    claim: \"C1 (causal validity)\"\n157\t    description: >\n158\t      [Dream A9] Non-ambiguity perturbation control arm to distinguish\n159\t      ambiguity-specific harm from general prompt brittleness.\n160\t      Generate 30 clause pairs with non-ambiguity perturbations:\n161\t      (a) 15 synonym substitution pairs (replace key terms with synonyms)\n162\t      (b) 15 clause reordering pairs (reorder conditions without changing meaning)\n163\t      Run 30 × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6) = 180 episodes.\n164\t      Key metric: Δ_net = Δ_ambiguity - Δ_perturb (net ambiguity-specific effect).\n165\t      [Reviewer升级] 必须在 plan_002/003 full study 之前完成——\n166\t      如果 perturbation Δpp ≈ ambiguity Δpp，2,400 episodes 全部无效。\n167\t      低成本验证（30 pairs + 120 episodes API）优先于高成本投入。\n168\t      [判定标准 — 5 档]:\n169\t      PASS: Δ_perturb < 5pp (CI含0), ratio < 0.15 → C1 因果 claim 最强形式\n170\t      PASS+caveat: 5-10pp, ratio 0.15-0.30 → 报告 perturbation baseline, C1 写 net effect\n171\t      CONDITIONAL: 10-15pp, ratio 0.30-0.45 → 需 Δ_net > 20pp 且显著才可发表\n172\t      WARNING: 15-20pp, ratio 0.45-0.60 → C1 改为 \"additional violations beyond sensitivity\"\n173\t      FAIL: > 20pp, ratio > 0.60 → 无法声称 ambiguity-specific, 需根本重新设计\n174\t      [Power 注意]: N=120 对 10pp 差异 power ≈ 30%. 用 CI 宽度判定, 非 p-value.\n175\t      若 CI 过宽(>15pp width), 追加 60 episodes 压窄至 <10pp width.\n176\t      输出标准化 verdict 文件: perturbation_Δpp, ambiguity_Δpp, net_Δpp, CI, ratio, verdict.\n177\t    priority: P0\n178\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n179\t    deps: [plan_001]\n180\t    status: planned\n181\t\n182\t  # === P2: Nice to have ===\n183\t\n184\t  - id: plan_008\n185\t    name: classifier_poc\n186\t    claim: \"practical contribution\"\n187\t    description: >\n188\t      Binary ambiguity detector PoC: fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-large on\n189\t      annotated clause pairs (ambiguous/unambiguous labels). Eval on\n190\t      held-out set. Demonstrates practical applicability of findings.\n191\t      Phase 3 from IDEA_BRIEF, scoped to PoC for EMNLP.\n192\t    priority: P2\n193\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n194\t    deps: [plan_001]\n195\t    status: planned\n196\t\n197\t# Resource summary:\n198\t# P0 GPU: 48h (plan_003 local inference)\n199\t# P1 GPU: 12h (plan_006 reliability)\n200\t# P2 GPU: 8h (plan_008 classifier fine-tuning)\n201\t# Total GPU: 68h on RTX PRO 6000\n202\t# API cost: ~$350-550 (1,800 main API + 1,200 local cross-judge + 720 reliability + 180 perturbation + judge cal)\n203\t# Models: gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6 (API) + Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ (local) = 5 total\n204\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd9ee42-9f53-44aa-92a5-74909781e0f9","uuid":"5f6b8cbe-a0fa-443f-b2df-6fdf80a7c0fd","timestamp":"2026-05-20T15:46:47.226Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/experiment_plan.yaml","content":"# Experiment Plan — policy_ambiguity_safety\n# Post-MVP, targeting EMNLP 2026 (ARR Aug cycle)\n# Claims reference paper_framing.md\n\nexperiments:\n  # === P0: Must-run for paper ===\n\n  - id: plan_001\n    name: full_study_clause_generation\n    claim: \"C1, C2, C3\"\n    description: >\n      Generate remaining clauses for full study: coreferential (50 new),\n      authorization_scope (50 new), lexical (+20 to reach 50),\n      incompleteness (+20 to reach 50). Total 140 new clauses.\n      Validate all 300 clauses (50/type × 6 types) for completeness\n      and cross-type balance. Mix CP format per Reviewer suggestion\n      (labeled + unlabeled).\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: []\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_001b\n    name: new_type_mini_pilot\n    claim: \"C1 (validation)\"\n    description: >\n      Mini-pilot for coreferential + authorization_scope (never tested):\n      5 clauses/type × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes.\n      Verify: (a) ambiguous triggers violations (b) unambiguous control < 15%.\n      If systematic issues found, fix clause design before full study.\n      API cost negligible (~$2). Per Reviewer warning on untested types.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_002\n    name: full_study_api\n    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4, C5\"\n    description: >\n      Run 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1,\n      claude-sonnet-4-6) = 1,800 episodes on τ²-bench. Cross-judge\n      evaluation. Output: episodes.jsonl + judgments.jsonl. No GPU needed.\n      Claude via OpenRouter proxy (base_url=http://47.94.22.126/v1).\n      [2026-05-20] Claude added per distill gap (4/8 papers use Claude baseline).\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_001b, plan_010]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_003\n    name: full_study_local\n    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4, C5\"\n    description: >\n      Run 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B,\n      Qwen3-32B-AWQ via vLLM) = 1,200 episodes on τ²-bench.\n      Requires 1× RTX PRO 6000 (48GB). Cross-judge uses API models.\n      Can run in parallel with plan_002.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 48\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_004\n    name: full_study_analysis\n    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4\"\n    description: >\n      Statistical analysis of full study data (3,000 episodes):\n      (a) Binary effect per type with bootstrap CI (C1)\n      (b) Omnibus χ² + pairwise across 6 types (C2)\n      (c) Visibility comparison: CP vs scopal rates (C3)\n      (d) Model × type interaction: 5×6 contingency + logistic regression (C4)\n      Report effect sizes + CI for all comparisons per Reviewer suggestion.\n      [Dream A3] Power analysis: report MDE for C2 (given N=250/type pooled)\n      and C3 (given N=250 per type). If V < 0.20 but MDE > observed V,\n      discuss underpowered possibility.\n      [Dream A4] TOST equivalence test with both ±15pp and ±10pp margins.\n      Justify margin choice explicitly.\n      [Dream A10] Report per-type information delta (token count difference\n      between ambiguous and unambiguous variants) as control variable.\n      [Dream B&K] Inter-model agreement on ambiguous clauses: do 5 models\n      adopt same or different interpretations? (supplementary analysis)\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_005\n    name: error_analysis\n    claim: \"C5\"\n    description: >\n      Qualitative analysis of agent traces from full study:\n      (a) Sample 50 violation traces per type (300 total)\n      (b) Classify failure modes (scope misapplication, conservative refusal,\n          assumption-based action, arbitrary rule selection, etc.)\n      (c) Cross-type failure mode distribution\n      (d) Visibility mechanism: compare CP traces (explicit conflict detection\n          behavior) vs scopal traces (surface scope adoption without awareness)\n      (e) Model-specific failure patterns (connect to C4)\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n    status: planned\n\n  # === P1: Important for robustness ===\n\n  - id: plan_006\n    name: reliability_test\n    claim: \"C1, C2\"\n    description: >\n      Test-retest reliability: select 30 representative clauses (5/type),\n      run 3 independent replicates × 2 conditions × 5 models = 900 episodes.\n      Compute ICC for per-clause violation rates. Addresses Reviewer warning\n      about ±8pp sampling noise (scopal 51.7% → 43.3% across MVP/diag).\n      Bootstrap CI width should be < 10pp for key comparisons.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_007\n    name: realism_validation\n    claim: \"C1 (methodological)\"\n    description: >\n      Validate synthetic ambiguity injection realism:\n      (a) Linguistic property comparison with DRIP-R natural ambiguities\n          (sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR) + KS tests\n      (b) Optional: discriminator test if DRIP-R data accessible\n      Addresses RC4 (ecological validity).\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_009\n    name: judge_calibration\n    claim: \"C1 (methodological)\"\n    description: >\n      LLM-as-judge calibration per distilled research norm (5/8 papers):\n      (a) Sample 100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition\n      (b) Human expert labels (2 annotators, target κ ≥ 0.75)\n      (c) Compute judge precision/recall/F1 against human ground truth\n      (d) Per-severity-tier agreement rates\n      (e) Report in Method section as standard practice per AgentAuditor/DRIP-R\n      [Dream A7] Upgraded P1→P0: Dream best-tier reviewers identified this\n      as \"single most critical missing validation.\" Without it, entire\n      measurement chain from episode to violation label is unvalidated.\n      κ=0.91 measures LLM-LLM agreement, not accuracy.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_002]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_010\n    name: perturbation_control\n    claim: \"C1 (causal validity)\"\n    description: >\n      [Dream A9] Non-ambiguity perturbation control arm to distinguish\n      ambiguity-specific harm from general prompt brittleness.\n      Generate 30 clause pairs with non-ambiguity perturbations:\n      (a) 15 synonym substitution pairs (replace key terms with synonyms)\n      (b) 15 clause reordering pairs (reorder conditions without changing meaning)\n      Run 30 × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6) = 180 episodes.\n      Key metric: Δ_net = Δ_ambiguity - Δ_perturb (net ambiguity-specific effect).\n      [Reviewer升级] 必须在 plan_002/003 full study 之前完成——\n      如果 perturbation Δpp ≈ ambiguity Δpp，2,400 episodes 全部无效。\n      低成本验证（30 pairs + 120 episodes API）优先于高成本投入。\n      [判定标准 — 5 档]:\n      PASS: Δ_perturb < 5pp (CI含0), ratio < 0.15 → C1 因果 claim 最强形式\n      PASS+caveat: 5-10pp, ratio 0.15-0.30 → 报告 perturbation baseline, C1 写 net effect\n      CONDITIONAL: 10-15pp, ratio 0.30-0.45 → 需 Δ_net > 20pp 且显著才可发表\n      WARNING: 15-20pp, ratio 0.45-0.60 → C1 改为 \"additional violations beyond sensitivity\"\n      FAIL: > 20pp, ratio > 0.60 → 无法声称 ambiguity-specific, 需根本重新设计\n      [Power 注意]: N=120 对 10pp 差异 power ≈ 30%. 用 CI 宽度判定, 非 p-value.\n      若 CI 过宽(>15pp width), 追加 60 episodes 压窄至 <10pp width.\n      输出标准化 verdict 文件: perturbation_Δpp, ambiguity_Δpp, net_Δpp, CI, ratio, verdict.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  # === P2: Nice to have ===\n\n  - id: plan_008\n    name: classifier_poc\n    claim: \"practical contribution\"\n    description: >\n      Binary ambiguity detector PoC: fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-large on\n      annotated clause pairs (ambiguous/unambiguous labels). Eval on\n      held-out set. Demonstrates practical applicability of findings.\n      Phase 3 from IDEA_BRIEF, scoped to PoC for EMNLP.\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n# Resource summary:\n# P0 GPU: 48h (plan_003 local inference)\n# P1 GPU: 12h (plan_006 reliability)\n# P2 GPU: 8h (plan_008 classifier fine-tuning)\n# Total GPU: 68h on RTX PRO 6000\n# API cost: ~$350-550 (1,800 main API + 1,200 local cross-judge + 720 reliability + 180 perturbation + judge cal)\n# Models: gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6 (API) + Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ (local) = 5 total\n","numLines":204,"startLine":1,"totalLines":204}}}
