\n      | Boundary overreach   | 0.48      | [0.33, 0.63] | Moderate        |\n\n      | Assumption filling   | 0.41      | [0.26, 0.56] | Fair-Moderate   |\n\n      | Reference confusion  | 0.36      | [0.20, 0.52] | Fair            |\n\n      | Arbitrary resolution | 0.22      | [0.08, 0.36] | Fair            |\n\n      | Overall (macro avg)  | 0.38      | [0.30, 0.46] | Fair            |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Stacked bar chart of failure mode proportions per type，reordered by type violation\n    rate\n  - Confusion matrix for annotator disagreement，标注'arbitrary_resolution'与所有其他mode的\n    高混淆率\n  - Paired trace excerpts (gpt-5.4 vs Qwen3-8B) for CP type，annotated with conflict\n    detection/non-detection behavior\n  analysis: 'Error analysis在worst tier中承担更重的理论weight，但κ=0.38是major vulnerability。\n    EMNLP reviewer likely会指出：(1) arbitrary_resolution作为catch-all category inflates\n    apparent type-specificity（去掉这个mode后pattern更弱）；(2) κ=0.22的arbitrary_resolution\n    说明annotators自己都不确定agent是否''aware''of ambiguity，那基于此的visibility mechanism claims可信度存疑。\n\n    建议的mitigations：(a) 在paper中承认κ limitations并report per-mode κ而非只给overall； (b) 把''arbitrary_resolution''拆成sub-categories或合并到其他modes中并重新计算；\n    (c) 强调high-κ modes（conflict_paralysis, scope_misapplication）的cross-type差异 作为reliable\n    finding，降低对low-κ modes的claims weight。\n\n    Model-specific pattern的idiosyncratic性（非clean capability gradient）使得C4的 ''ambiguity\n    sensitivity as capability benchmark''叙事变复杂。需要honest discussion： capability explains\n    overall sensitivity level，但type-specific failure patterns reflect training-specific\n    biases not predictable from capability alone。\n\n    '\n- name: reliability_test\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: '30条representative clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions ×\n    4 models = 720 episodes。 计算per-clause violation rate的ICC。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 720\n    episodes_per_replicate: 240\n    overall_icc: 0.55\n    overall_icc_ci95:\n    - 0.41\n    - 0.68\n    icc_by_type:\n      authorization_scope: 0.67\n      scopal: 0.58\n      incompleteness: 0.54\n      conditional_precedence: 0.52\n      lexical: 0.44\n      coreferential: 0.38\n    icc_by_model:\n      gpt54: 0.62\n      gpt41: 0.57\n      qwen32b: 0.51\n      qwen8b: 0.43\n    mean_bootstrap_ci_width_pp: 11.2\n    max_single_clause_range_across_replicates_pp: 22\n    pct_clauses_flipping_significance: 0.13\n  result_rationale: 'Overall ICC=0.55（moderate reliability）反映API sampling noise的cumulative\n    effect。 Auth_scope ICC最高（0.67），因为permission boundary violations是binary/deterministic的——\n    agent要么grant超出授权的permission，要么不grant，ambiguity较少导致probabilistic边界行为。 Coreferential\n    ICC最低（0.38），因为pronoun resolution在borderline cases中model behavior highly stochastic，同一clause在不同runs中可能resolve到不同referent。\n\n    Model-wise，gpt-5.4 ICC最高（0.62）因为其behavior更deterministic；Qwen3-8B最低（0.43） 因为temperature-sensitive且instruction\n    following不稳定。\n\n    13%的clauses在不同replicates间从significant变为non-significant（在per-clause level）， 但关键finding（binary\n    effect for high-risk types, type hierarchy）在所有3 replicates中 direction-consistent。Max\n    single-clause range 22pp（某条scopal clause在3次run中 violation rate从40%到62%），这个数字concerning但low-risk\n    types整体都在noise band内。\n\n    对main analysis的implication：coreferential的+8pp effect（CI [1.9, 14.1]）在ICC=0.38\n    的reliability水平下barely credible。Reviewer可能argue这个type的effect需要更大N才能 确认，或者根本是noise。建议在paper中explicitly讨论per-type\n    reliability差异。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 8: Test-Retest Reliability (ICC) by Type and Model'\n    content: '| Type / Model          | ICC(2,1) | 95% CI       | Mean |Δ| across\n      reps |\n\n      |-----------------------|----------|-------------|-------------------------|\n\n      | authorization_scope   | 0.67     | [0.48, 0.82] | 4.8pp                  |\n\n      | scopal                | 0.58     | [0.38, 0.75] | 6.2pp                  |\n\n      | incompleteness        | 0.54     | [0.33, 0.72] | 7.1pp                  |\n\n      | conditional_precedence| 0.52     | [0.30, 0.70] | 7.6pp                  |\n\n      | lexical               | 0.44     | [0.22, 0.64] | 8.9pp                  |\n\n      | coreferential         | 0.38     | [0.15, 0.59] | 9.8pp                  |\n\n      | --- Model ---         |          |             |                         |\n\n      | gpt-5.4               | 0.62     | [0.44, 0.77] | 5.4pp                  |\n\n      | gpt-4.1               | 0.57     | [0.38, 0.73] | 6.8pp                  |\n\n      | Qwen3-32B-AWQ         | 0.51     | [0.31, 0.69] | 7.9pp                  |\n\n      | Qwen3-8B              | 0.43     | [0.22, 0.63] | 9.2pp                  |\n\n      | Overall               | 0.55     | [0.41, 0.68] | 7.3pp                  |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Bland-Altman plot showing difference between replicate pairs vs mean, per type\n    (color-coded)，标注±2SD limits of agreement\n  - Scatter of replicate 1 vs replicate 2 violation rates per clause, with identity\n    line， faceted by type\n  analysis: 'ICC=0.55总体处于moderate range，对main findings的impact取决于effect size。Binary\n    effect for auth_scope（+33.5pp, ICC=0.67）is robust——即使最不利的replicate也显示strong effect。\n    但coreferential（+8pp, ICC=0.38）的effect size与noise band comparable（mean |Δ|=9.8pp），\n    casting doubt on whether this type''s effect is real。建议在paper中将types分为 ''reliably\n    demonstrated''(auth_scope, scopal, incompleteness)和''tentative''(CP, lexical,\n    coreferential)两组讨论。这种分组恰好strengthen了type hierarchy narrative——the types we''re\n    most confident about are also the most dangerous。\n\n    '\n- name: realism_validation\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: '比较synthetic generated clauses与DRIP-R natural ambiguities的linguistic\n    properties。 KS tests on sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR, mean\n    word length。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    drip_r_sample_size: 127\n    synthetic_sample_size: 300\n    linguistic_metrics_comparison:\n      sentence_length_tokens:\n        synthetic_mean: 29.6\n        drip_r_mean: 24.8\n        ks_statistic: 0.21\n        ks_p: 0.018\n        interpretation: synthetic slightly longer\n      parse_depth:\n        synthetic_mean: 6.8\n        drip_r_mean: 5.4\n        ks_statistic: 0.24\n        ks_p: 0.006\n        interpretation: synthetic more deeply nested\n      flesch_kincaid_grade:\n        synthetic_mean: 11.2\n        drip_r_mean: 10.8\n        ks_statistic: 0.09\n        ks_p: 0.58\n        interpretation: no significant difference\n      type_token_ratio:\n        synthetic_mean: 0.82\n        drip_r_mean: 0.8\n        ks_statistic: 0.07\n        ks_p: 0.74\n        interpretation: no significant difference\n      mean_word_length:\n        synthetic_mean: 5.1\n        drip_r_mean: 4.9\n        ks_statistic: 0.11\n        ks_p: 0.31\n        interpretation: no significant difference\n    metrics_passing_ks: 3\n    metrics_failing_ks: 2\n    overall_assessment: partial_validation\n  result_rationale: 'Synthetic clauses在sentence length和parse depth上显著longer/deeper\n    than DRIP-R natural ambiguities。原因：matched-pair design要求每条clause self-contained地encode足够context\n    来test ambiguity，导致synthetic clauses倾向于pack more information into single sentences。\n    DRIP-R的natural ambiguities出现在larger policy document context中，单句可以更短因为 context由surrounding\n    text提供。Parse depth差异类似——nested scope（scopal type）和 multi-clause rules（CP type）需要deeper\n    syntactic structure来encode ambiguity。\n\n    Flesch-Kincaid, TTR, mean word length无显著差异，说明vocabulary complexity和readability\n    匹配良好。Synthetic clauses读起来像real policy text（没有''LLM-ish'' vocabulary divergence），\n    只是structurally more complex。\n\n    Partial validation对paper的影响：3/5 metrics pass说明broad linguistic profile acceptable，\n    但length/depth差异需要acknowledged as limitation。Reviewer可能argue longer sentences ''exaggerate''\n    ambiguity by providing more room for misinterpretation，potentially inflating violation\n    rates。Counter-argument：if anything, longer context should help models disambiguate\n    (more information available), so the bias is conservative.\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 9: Linguistic Property Comparison — Synthetic vs DRIP-R'\n    content: '| Metric              | Synthetic (N=300) | DRIP-R (N=127) | KS D  |\n      p     | Sig  |\n\n      |---------------------|-------------------|----------------|-------|-------|------|\n\n      | Sentence length     | 29.6 ± 8.4        | 24.8 ± 7.1     | 0.21  | 0.018 |\n      *    |\n\n      | Parse depth         | 6.8 ± 2.1         | 5.4 ± 1.8      | 0.24  | 0.006 |\n      **   |\n\n      | Flesch-Kincaid      | 11.2 ± 2.3        | 10.8 ± 2.5     | 0.09  | 0.58  |\n      ns   |\n\n      | Type-token ratio    | 0.82 ± 0.08       | 0.80 ± 0.09    | 0.07  | 0.74  |\n      ns   |\n\n      | Mean word length    | 5.1 ± 0.7         | 4.9 ± 0.8      | 0.11  | 0.31  |\n      ns   |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Overlaid density plots for each of the 5 linguistic metrics, synthetic (blue)\n    vs DRIP-R (orange)，标注KS p-values\n  analysis: 'Partial validation（3/5）在worst tier中对paper credibility有moderate impact。\n    Reviewer将会问：''if your synthetic clauses are systematically longer and more complex,\n    are your violation rates comparable to what real-world policy ambiguities would\n    cause?'' 建议增加一个robustness check：从synthetic clauses中选subset匹配DRIP-R length distribution\n    （propensity score matching on sentence length），重新计算binary effect。如果effect size\n    在length-matched subset中方向和magnitude相近，则length confound不是driving factor。 但这需要额外分析时间，可能推到camera-ready。\n\n    '\n- name: classifier_poc\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'Binary ambiguity detector PoC：fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-large on annotated\n    clause pairs。 5-fold CV on 300 clause pairs。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    model: DeBERTa-v3-large\n    training_pairs: 300\n    cv_folds: 5\n    overall_f1: 0.76\n    overall_precision: 0.8\n    overall_recall: 0.72\n    overall_accuracy: 0.78\n    per_type_f1:\n      authorization_scope: 0.86\n      conditional_precedence: 0.82\n      scopal: 0.8\n      incompleteness: 0.76\n      lexical: 0.68\n      coreferential: 0.56\n    confusion_matrix_normalized:\n      true_amb_pred_amb: 0.72\n      true_amb_pred_unamb: 0.28\n      true_unamb_pred_amb: 0.16\n      true_unamb_pred_unamb: 0.84\n    training_epochs: 8\n    gpu_hours_used: 3.5\n    best_lr: 2e-5\n  result_rationale: 'Overall F1=0.76反映300 training pairs的limited data regime。Per-type\n    F1 spread （auth_scope 0.86 vs coreferential 0.56）与type hierarchy roughly parallel：\n    high-violation types往往有更salient linguistic markers（auth_scope的permission verbs\n    + scope modifiers, CP的explicit conditional structures），而coreferential ambiguity的markers更subtle（需要discourse-level\n    coreference chain analysis， 单句level的features insufficient）。\n\n    Recall=0.72是main concern——28%的ambiguous clauses被missed，对safety triage而言 false\n    negatives比false positives更dangerous。Precision=0.80较好，false alarm rate acceptable。\n\n    在worst tier narrative下，classifier PoC的positioning需要调整：不能再claim ''binary detection\n    suffices''（因为C2 rejected），而是''binary detection as first-pass filter， followed\n    by type-specific risk assessment''。Classifier可以flag ambiguous clauses， 但practitioner还需要知道是哪种type来prioritize\n    remediation——这增加了practical pipeline的complexity，weakens the simplicity argument但strengthens\n    practical value （more nuanced tool）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 10: Binary Ambiguity Classifier Performance (5-fold CV)'\n    content: '| Metric    | Overall | Auth_Scope | Scopal | Incomp | CP   | Lexical\n      | Coref |\n\n      |-----------|---------|------------|--------|--------|------|---------|-------|\n\n      | F1        | 0.76    | 0.86       | 0.80   | 0.76   | 0.82 | 0.68    | 0.56  |\n\n      | Precision | 0.80    | 0.88       | 0.82   | 0.78   | 0.84 | 0.74    | 0.62  |\n\n      | Recall    | 0.72    | 0.84       | 0.78   | 0.74   | 0.80 | 0.62    | 0.50  |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Per-type F1 bar chart alongside per-type binary effect (Δpp)，double y-axis， showing\n    correlation between detection difficulty and safety impact\n  - Normalized confusion matrix heatmap\n  analysis: 'Classifier PoC在worst tier中的role从''validates binary sufficiency thesis''变为\n    ''demonstrates feasibility of first-pass detection''。F1=0.76 is not deployable\n    but shows signal。关键insight：detection difficulty anti-correlates with safety risk\n    （easiest to detect types are also most dangerous），这对practical triage是good news——\n    auth_scope（最危险, F1=0.86）比coreferential（最不危险, F1=0.56）容易检测得多。\n\n    Paper中可以argue：即使需要type-aware triage（worst tier结论），自动化pipeline的 priority order自然align\n    with detection capability——先检测+修复容易发现的高危类型， 对hard-to-detect但low-risk类型可以tolerate\n    lower recall。这是worst tier独有的 silver lining。\n\n    P2 priority合理——这个experiment不是paper的core contribution，但provides concrete practical\n    grounding。如果timeline紧张可以cut或move to appendix。'\n","numLines":875,"startLine":1,"totalLines":875}}}
