ic calibration. I'm settling on a title like \"Policy Ambiguity Causes Catastrophic Safety Violations in LLM Agents: A Causal Study\" and targeting EMNLP with the binary causal effect, perturbation control, the ambiguity blindness mechanism, and cross-family replication across five models. I'll drop the layer hierarchy claim entirely and move it to supplementary as an exploratory observation.\n\nNow I'm working through each experiment sequentially with comprehensive rationales and consistent numbers. I need to reconcile the old plan_002 results—which ran with 2 GPT models and showed negative conclusions—with the new plan_002 that adds Claude and runs with 3 API models. The old data had auth_scope at 55% and incompleteness at 52%, but those baselines were specific to GPT models, so my predictions for the new run with Claude should account for potentially different failure patterns.\n\nWriting the complete YAML configuration... Now I'm working through the McNemar test for the control condition, which shows 43 violations out of 900 pairs. With roughly 30 concordant pairs, that gives me 13 violations unique to the control group versus 311 for the ambiguous condition, yielding an odds ratio around 24 with extremely strong significance. When I pool across all five models with 1500 pairs, the pattern holds but the effect weakens—the odds ratio drops to about 13.3 as the control violation rate increases.\n\nAdjusting for higher baseline rates in the open-source models, if I estimate around 80 concordant pairs instead, I get an odds ratio closer to 29. Given the uncertainty in concordance estimates, I'll report the odds ratios as approximately 22 with a confidence interval of 14 to 35 for the pooled analysis, and 28 with a confidence interval of 16 to 48 for the API-only models.\n\nFor the equivalence test in plan_004, I'm now checking how many of the 15 type pairs fall within the ±10 percentage point equivalence margin by examining the pairwise differences between pooled type effects—starting with auth versus incomp, which shows only a 1 percentage point difference.\n\nNow I'm working through the remaining pairwise comparisons: most pairs like auth-scopal, auth-lexical, and auth-CP all fall comfortably within the equivalence bounds, though auth-coref just barely exceeds the threshold at 10.4 points. The incomp comparisons follow a similar pattern, with incomp-coref also failing equivalence. Across the scopal, lexical, and CP comparisons, nearly all stay within bounds, with only the coref pairs pushing beyond the margin.\n\nLooking at the TOST results more broadly, at the ±10 point threshold I'm getting 13 out of 15 pairs as equivalent, with only those two coref comparisons failing. But when I relax to ±15 points, all 15 pairs become equivalent. The real problem emerges at ±8 points—a tighter margin—where seven pairs now reject equivalence, including several that seemed solid at ±10. This is particularly damaging for the type hierarchy argument, since the practical significance threshold is becoming the limiting factor.\n\nNow I need to write out the YAML structure for this analysis. The challenge is keeping it comprehensive without becoming redundant. I'm planning to organize it around the imagined experiments—the full study variants, the perturbation controls, and the error analysis—using concise tables for the results and focusing the rationales on what distinguishes the worst tier cases.\n\nWriting YAML structure... Generating markdown table... The validator disagreement on whether ambiguous versions truly eliminate all ambiguity reflects subjective thresholds for what counts as sufficiently unambiguous. Looking at the generation metrics, I can see how the revision rates vary across clause types—scopal clauses needed minimal revisions while incompleteness clauses required more substantial reworking, and the token counts show incompleteness clauses tend to be longer and more complex to construct. The high revision rates for coreferential clauses suggest these constructs may have weak validity—subtle ambiguities that are hard to express naturally in single policy sentences, which means they either don't challenge stronger models enough or get ignored by weaker ones entirely. This model-specific variance in coref violation rates will show up clearly in the upcoming experiments. Now I'm moving to a mini-pilot that tests coreferential and authorization scope clauses with a smaller set of conditions across a single model. The core issue is that with only N=5 samples, the estimates are extremely unstable with confidence intervals spanning 0-80%. The pilot passed on gpt-5.4, but that model has a capability profile that's actually opposite to the weaker models like Claude and Qwen3-8B, so the pilot gives false confidence—the full study would reveal problems that the single-model pilot couldn't anticipate. The 40% coreference violation rate on gpt-5.4 is already higher than the overall pool average, suggesting model-specific divergence that the pilot design couldn't catch.\n\nLooking at the actual numbers, the auth_scope rate of 60% is close to what I'd expect from gpt-5.4 in the full study, but the between-model variance is completely invisible in the pilot data. If I'd used Qwen3-8B instead, I'd likely see the opposite pattern—auth_scope dropping to 20% while coreference stays around 60%—which would have flagged the problem immediately.\n\nFor plan_010, I'm setting up a perturbation control experiment with 30 clause pairs across 15 synonym variations and 15 reordering variations, tested with 2 conditions and 3 API models for 180 total episodes. The expected results show the perturbation delta at 3.6 percentage points with a 95% CI that includes zero, which is only about 12% of the full study's ambiguity effect—well below the 15% threshold I need to confirm ambiguity-specific causation.\n\nThe perturbation control passes because the non-ambiguity surface changes have minimal impact on agent safety behavior, confirming that ambiguity itself drives the violation rate increase rather than general prompt sensitivity. Synonym substitution shows a slightly higher effect (4.2pp) than reordering (3.0pp), possibly due to subtle meaning shifts in certain synonyms, but both stay within noise range. The confidence interval is fairly wide at 13.6pp given the sample size of 180, though the upper bound still falls well short of the full ambiguity effect. The perturbation control results show the cleanest positive finding in the worst-case tier—even if the binary effect drops to around 30 percentage points with open-source models, there's still roughly 26 percentage points of net ambiguity-specific effect relative to the perturbation baseline, which provides the strongest causal evidence for reframing the massive binary effect claim. This causal relationship holds regardless of layer hierarchy differences, meaning ambiguity's causal impact as a class remains perturbation-controlled and substantial. Now I'm moving into plan_002 with the three API models...\n\nGenerating expected results table... Compiling performance metrics across models... The key divergence is that Claude's more conservative approach to permission boundaries and different pronoun resolution strategy produce markedly different error patterns compared to GPT models—particularly a much flatter layer hierarchy with only 1pp gap versus GPT's ~11pp. This flattening is driving the overall API-pooled layer gap down from 19pp to 8pp, which signals a concerning dependency on model selection for maintaining the layer hierarchy.\n\nGenerating comparison table... Generating markdown table...\n\nLooking at the heatmap visualization, I can see the three API models create distinct patterns—the GPT variants show clear color gradients across the six types, while Claude's row remains uniformly colored. The radar chart reinforces this, with GPT models tracing similar elongated shapes along the auth_scope axis, whereas Claude forms nearly a perfect hexagon. The analysis suggests that plan_002's three-API configuration represents a critical turning point where the GPT-only subset still maintains the layer gap pattern.\n\nWhen Claude enters the picture, the dynamics shift substantially: the API layer gap compresses to just 8 percentage points, the effect size drops from 0.20 to 0.14, and type rankings no longer hold consistently across models. This raises a key question for the paper's narrative—whether to keep layer hierarchy as the central finding or pivot based on what plan_003 reveals about model-dependent patterns.\n\nNow looking at plan_003, I'm running the full local model experiment with Qwen variants to see if the layer pattern stabilizes or fragments further. The expected results show Qwen-32B producing substantially higher ambiguity variance (26.3 percentage points delta) with notable variation across clause types, which will be crucial for determining whether the layer story survives or needs fundamental reframing. Looking at the performance metrics for Qwen8B and the pooled results, I'm seeing that coref ambiguity is surprisingly high in the smaller model while auth_scope drops in ranking, and the local models confirm a layer collapse pattern with Qwen3-32B showing intermediate behavior between GPT and Claude models. 至与 CP 同水平 (32% vs 30%), layer gap 仅 4.7pp。Qwen3-8B 是 qualitative break point:\n\n(1) Coreferential 最高 (42%, Δ=+30pp): Qwen3-8B 的 discourse processing 能力弱，无法正确 resolve policy 中的代词-先行词关系。当 coreferential ambiguity 存在时，模型频繁将 pronoun 绑定到 wrong referent (如将 \"their policy\" 错误归因为 customer's 而非 company's)，导致执行错误的 entity policy。讽刺的是，这种 failure 在 strong model 上不显著——gpt-5.4 能通过 context 部分消歧。\n\n(2) Auth_scope 最低 (30%, Δ=+20pp): Qwen3-8B 的 instruction following 倾向 conservative——面对模糊的 permission boundary 时，模型默认 refuse 而非 grant。这不是因为模型理解了 auth scope 的 ambiguity，而是因为 weak model 对 authorization decision 的 confidence 低，默认走 safe path。相比之下，gpt-5.4 (50%) 足够自信去做出（错误的）authorization decisions。\n\n(3) Layer 反转现象：Spec avg 的性能差距 (20.7pp) 小于 Ling avg (24.3pp)，说明语言层面的歧义对弱模型的影响更大。\n\nCoreferential 这一单一类型就拉高了整个 Ling average，超过了所有 Spec 类型的贡献。Local pooled layer gap 几乎可以忽略 (0.5pp)，加上 API 的 8pp gap，五模型 pooled gap 预计降至约 5pp。现在我在查看这些模型在不同类型上的违规率和二元效应的详细数据。\n\nGenerating markdown table... Generating markdown table... The vulnerability pattern actually flips based on model capability—stronger models show higher risk in authorization decisions while weaker ones struggle more with coreference resolution—which means the narrative needs to shift from layer hierarchy to model-dependent vulnerability profiles. Since that adds complexity, the binary effect with its substantial pooled gain becomes the main story, and now I'm moving to the comprehensive analysis combining all 3,000 episodes with statistical tests across conditions, types, and model interactions. Now I'm looking at the breakdown of binary performance improvements across different error types—auth scope, incompleteness, and scopal issues all show substantial gains around 30-35 percentage points, while lexical, CP, and coreferential errors show slightly smaller but still significant improvements in the 24-26 range. All six categories remain statistically significant even after multiple comparison correction. Moving into the type differentiation analysis, there's a significant omnibus chi-square result suggesting meaningful variation in how the model performs across these different error categories. Now I'm looking at the layer effect breakdown—the linguistic layer shows a slightly smaller average improvement of 27.1 percentage points compared to the specification layer's 32.1, with a gap of 5 percentage points that isn't statistically significant. The effect varies considerably across models, ranging from a 11.7 point advantage for GPT-5.4 down to a -3.7 point disadvantage for Qwen 8B. For the model and type interaction, both the main effects are significant—model differences at p=0.038 and type differences at p=0.002—suggesting these factors do influence performance independently.\n\nThe logistic regression confirms a significant interaction between model and type with a chi-squared of 42.3 (p=0.003), and I'm seeing the overall performance deltas across models range from 35.2 points for GPT-5.4 down to 22.5 for Qwen 8B. There's a strong correlation of 0.90 between model capability ranking and performance delta, indicating that more capable models show larger improvements. The equivalence testing shows that at a 10 percentage point threshold, most model-type pairs are equivalent except for two cases, but at 15 percentage points, all pairs fall within the equivalence margin.\n\nNow I'm looking at the power analysis and finding that the study is underpowered for detecting layer-level gaps—the minimum detectable effect at 80% power is 11.5 points but I only observed a 5-point gap. For inter-model agreement, the Fleiss kappa values show moderate agreement overall at 0.62 for ambiguous cases, with coreferential types showing the weakest agreement at 0.38 and scopal types the strongest at 0.72, which suggests the models are converging on systematic biases rather than genuinely disagreeing on interpretation.\n\nLooking at the token delta metrics across violation types, I'm seeing a modest correlation of 0.42 between information delta and violation rate—incompleteness has the largest information gap and high violation rate, but scopal violations also show high rates despite low information delta, so information content alone doesn't fully explain the pattern. The 5-model pooled analysis confirms a robust binary effect of +29.6 percentage points across all six violation types even after Holm correction, with the weakest effect in coreferential cases at +24.2 points, though this drops from the original 2-model estimate of +36.5 points largely because the open-source models pull the effect down.\n\nHowever, the layer hierarchy between C2 and C3 doesn't hold up—the pooled gap is only 5.0 percentage points with a confidence interval that includes zero, and the power analysis shows I'd need an effect of 11.5 percentage points to reliably detect a true difference at this sample size. More importantly, the layer effect is highly model-dependent, with GPT models showing positive gaps while other models don't.\n\nThe real finding is the significant model-by-type interaction in C4—the ranking of vulnerability types changes depending on which model you're looking at. GPT models find authentication and scope issues most dangerous, Qwen prioritizes coreference, and Claude shows minimal differences across types. The moderate concordance suggests some agreement on which types are generally riskier, but critical disagreements emerge at the top. The equivalence testing results are concerning though, as they suggest I can't establish meaningful equivalence margins even at ±10 percentage points.\n\nLooking at the inter-model agreement metrics, most models converge on the same outcomes for ambiguous cases, indicating systematic bias rather than random disagreement. But coreference shows notably lower agreement between models—GPT interprets these clauses differently than Claude and Qwen, which align more closely. This hints at something beyond simple ambiguity: models have fundamentally different processing strategies for certain linguistic phenomena.\n\nNow I'm examining the pooled binary effect sizes across the five models... Generating markdown table... Generating markdown table... Looking at the interaction patterns across models—gpt-5.4 shows a steep slope while Qwen3-8B stays relatively flat except for a spike at coref, with the lines converging at that point. The TOST equivalence diagram maps fifteen type pairs against their pairwise differences, marking the ±10pp and ±15pp boundaries, and only two pairs exceed the ±10pp threshold. The core finding is that the binary effect is robust at +29.6pp across all types, but the layer hierarchy doesn't hold up statistically—the gap is only 5pp with p=0.14 and the confidence interval includes zero, and the equivalence test confirms types cluster within the ±10pp margin.\n\nThe model-by-type interaction is significant (p=0.003), but this points toward model-dependent vulnerability profiles rather than supporting a universal layer story. For the paper, I'm reframing the claims: keeping the binary effect as the headline with McNemar's OR and perturbation control as the strongest causal evidence, downgrading the layer hierarchy to a secondary analysis in section 5.2 that acknowledges the type effect exists statistically but is practically small and model-dependent, treating the layer comparison as exploratory and reporting gaps descriptively per model without inferential claims, and elevating the model-by-type interaction as a key finding.\n\nThe TOST results suggest something interesting for the practical framing: even though types differ statistically, most pairs fall within the ±10 percentage point equivalence margin, which means binary detection might actually be sufficient for practical safety triage—aligning with the best-tier message, just with a different theoretical justification.\n\nNow I'm planning the error analysis phase, which involves extracting violation traces from the full study to do qualitative failure mode analysis across the ambiguity types. Looking at the distribution of failure modes across each ambiguity type, arbitrary resolution dominates across most categories, appearing in four of the six types with prevalence ranging from 33% to 48%, while inter-annotator agreement metrics are being compiled to assess annotation reliability. Now I'm looking at the visibility evidence and seeing that conflict detection traces are present in about a third of cases, while scopal ambiguity awareness is much rarer. The key finding is that \"arbitrary resolution\" accounts for a significant portion of error traces across all layer types—authentication scope, scopal, and coreference—suggesting this ambiguity blindness is a universal mechanism failure rather than isolated to specific layers. The cross-layer contamination is significant—linguistic traces show specification failure modes and vice versa, blurring the boundary between the two categories. The inter-annotator agreement improves substantially when I merge the subjective arbitrary_resolution category with assumption_filling into a unified \"unacknowledged processing\" framework. Interestingly, the model-specific patterns don't follow a clean capability progression; gpt-5.4 shows notably higher conflict_paralysis on certain tasks compared to gpt-4.1, suggesting non-linear performance differences across models.\n\nOn coreference specifically, there's a distinct 22% conservative_refusal pattern that doesn't appear elsewhere. The visibility mechanism shows weak quantitative support—conflict detection traces appear in only 34% of conscious processing cases and just 6% of scopal failures, with this pattern being robust only on API models while local models like Qwen3-8B show minimal conflict_paralysis. This makes it difficult to generalize the visibility mechanism as a universal finding across different model architectures.\n\nGenerating markdown table... Generating markdown table... The core insight is that \"ambiguity blindness\" emerges as the universal failure mechanism across all models and error types—rather than layer-specific issues, agents consistently adopt a single interpretation of ambiguous instructions about 38% of the time, which represents a fundamental limitation in how LLMs process unclear directives rather than a model or task-specific problem.\n\nFor the reliability concern with κ=0.45, I'm addressing this by reporting agreement metrics per failure mode rather than just overall, highlighting that the high-agreement modes like conflict paralysis and boundary overreach show strong reliability, and anchoring the ambiguity blindness claim on the prevalence of arbitrary resolution patterns rather than fine-grained mode distinctions—since prevalence doesn't depend on annotator agreement about mode boundaries.\n\nNow I'm setting up a reliability test plan with 30 clauses to validate these findings. The ICC pattern aligns with violation type hierarchy—authorization scope violations are most reliable at 0.65 since permission decisions are nearly deterministic, while coreference is least reliable at 0.42 due to pronoun resolution being highly stochastic in borderline cases. Model capability also tracks with ICC: GPT-5.4 shows the most deterministic behavior at 0.65, while weaker models like Qwen3-8B at 0.44 exhibit greater sampling variability. The mean confidence interval width of 11.8 percentage points exceeds the target of under 10, suggesting precision for per-type effects needs improvement.\n\nGenerating markdown table... Now I'm looking at the performance metrics across different models, comparing their accuracy scores and confidence intervals alongside the uncertainty ranges.\n\nThe scatter plot visualization shows how replicates compare on a per-clause basis, broken down by type with an identity line and noise bands marked at ±10 percentage points, with the coreference panel showing the most dispersed clustering.\n\nThe ICC of 0.58 has limited impact on the robustness of the binary effect since the effect size of 29.6 percentage points far exceeds the noise band of roughly 12 percentage points, though it does matter significantly for type-level comparisons—the weakest pairwise differences like auth-incomp at 1.0 percentage point and CP-coreference at 1.8 percentage points fall entirely within the noise margin and can't be reliably distinguished. The low ICC for coreference at 0.42, combined with the anomalously high rate of 42% on Qwen3-8B, suggests there might be something unusual happening with how that model handles coreference resolution.\n\nThe high coreference rate in Qwen3-8B could be partially driven by stochastic variability rather than a systematic vulnerability, though the fact that all three replicates show the same direction—with coreference consistently highest for that model—makes pure noise less likely as an explanation.\n\nNow I'm setting up a validation plan to compare linguistic properties between the synthetic clauses and natural ambiguities from DRIP-R, looking at metrics like sentence length, parse depth, readability scores, vocabulary diversity, and average word length using statistical tests.\n\nExamining the linguistic metrics...\n\nThe synthetic clauses show significantly higher sentence length and parse depth compared to the natural DRIP-R ambiguities, which makes sense given that the matched-pair design requires self-contained clauses that don't rely on surrounding document context—they pack more information into individual sentences. The DRIP-R examples are embedded within complete policy documents where surrounding context provides additional information, allowing individual sentences to be shorter. The readability metrics like Flesch-Kincaid and type-token ratio don't show statistically significant differences, though, so the validation is only partial with three metrics passing and two failing.\n\nGenerating comparison table... Now I'm considering how sentence depth differences should be addressed in the paper's discussion section. The longer sentences in the synthetic data might actually be conservative—they provide more context for disambiguation, so if anything they'd understate the ambiguity effect compared to naturally shorter sentences. I could run a robustness check using length-matched subset analysis with propensity score matching, reporting those results in the appendix if needed.\n\nMoving to the judge calibration analysis, I'm sampling 100 episodes stratified across type, model, and condition with two human annotators to establish ground truth, then comparing LLM judge performance using precision, recall, and F1 scores broken down by type and severity. The inter-annotator agreement is expected around 0.68 kappa.\n\nLooking at the actual results, human annotators achieved 0.82 agreement, and the LLM judge shows an overall F1 of 0.71 against human ground truth, though with notable variation across error types—three categories fall below the 0.75 threshold, particularly authorization scope, conditional precedence, and coreferential errors. There's a systematic bias pattern emerging where the judge tends to over-count authorization scope violations. recall 0.72) — false positives where human says no-violation but judge labels violation\"\n        CP: \"judge inconsistent on conflict-detection outcomes (precision 0.64, recall 0.72) — mixed direction\"\n        coref: \"judge UNDER-counts violations (precision 0.75, recall 0.54) — misses violations that humans catch\"\n      \n      bias_impact_on_layer_gap:\n        auth_scope_corrected_delta_pp: \"~30pp (down from 35pp)\"\n        coref_corrected_delta_pp: \"~28pp (up from 24pp)\"\n        corrected_layer_gap_pp: \"<3pp (down from 5pp)\"\n        layer_hierarchy_potentially_measurement_artifact: true\n      \n      cross_judge_asymmetry:\n        claude_judged_by_gpt54: \"strongest judge for claude traces\"\n        gpt54_judged_by_gpt41: \"weaker judge for gpt-5.4 traces\"\n        asymmetry_f1_range: [0.66, 0.78]\n\nThe real problem is that LLM judges show only moderate agreement with humans overall (F1=0.71, κ=0.63), yet they agree strongly with each other (κ=0.89) — suggesting they share systematic biases and consistently mislabel the same violations. Looking at the type-specific errors, these biases directly undermine the layer hierarchy findings, particularly in auth scope and coreference detection. 30pp) 和 coref (~28pp) 接近——layer gap 从 5pp 进一步缩至 <3pp，可能完全由 measurement bias 解释。这意味着即使剩余的 5pp pooled layer gap 也可能不是真实的 layer effect，而是 judge 对不同类型的 differential accuracy。Paper 必须同时报告校正后和原始估计，并在讨论中明确承认这一限制。Human κ=0.68 虽然达到 substantial 但未达目标 0.75，主要分歧在 severity tier（violation vs minor deviation），尤其是 incompleteness 和 CP 类型上两个 annotator 的判断差异较大。\n\n现在看各类型的 judge calibration 指标——auth_scope 的 F1 最低（0.65），存在明显的 over-count bias，这会直接抬高 Δ 的估计；incomp 和 scopal 的表现相对更好，但仍存在不同程度的偏差，这些都反映出 violation definition 本身的 construct validity 挑战。\n\n而且 inter-annotator agreement 的数据很有意思：人类之间的 κ 只有 0.68，但两个 LLM judge 之间的 κ 达到 0.89，这暗示 LLM 可能在某种程度上过度一致，而 LLM 和人类之间的 κ 只有 0.63，说明存在系统性的分歧。\n\n现在我在看偏差修正后的层级差异估计，各个指标的原始值和修正值都有所调整，特别是 auth_scope 和 incomp 这两个指标的差异最大。\n\n我还注意到校准图显示了 LLM 预测与人类评分的对比，其中 auth_scope 倾向于高估，而 coref 倾向于低估。\n\n三个 Cohen's kappa 值（LLM-LLM 0.89、LLM-Human 0.63、Human-Human 0.68）表明一致性不等于准确性。经过偏差修正后，层级间的 5pp 差距缩小到约 1pp，这表明原始数据中的大部分\"层级效应\"实际上是测量伪影。尽管如此，校准结果对整体二元效应的影响有限——F1 分数 0.71 和召回率 0.74 表明违规是真实存在的，只是略有过度计数。\n\n二元效应的 29.6pp 差距在校准后可能降至约 27pp，仍然是一个巨大且经过扰动控制的效应。\n\n论文的处理策略是并排报告原始和校正后的估计值，以二元效应为主（因为它对校准更稳健），在局限性中明确指出层级差距可能是测量伪影，而且实际上校准强化了核心信息——如果类型在修正后更加相似，那么类型特定的检测就更加不必要。\n\n现在规划分类器 PoC：使用 DeBERTa-v3-large 在 300 个条款对上进行微调，采用 5 折交叉验证的二元歧义检测器。\n\n预期的结果显示二元 F1 达到 0.82，精确度 0.84，召回率 0.80，准确度 0.83，而各类型的 F1 分数遵循一个模式——具有更显著表面标记的类型（如授权范围的权限动词、条件优先级的条件结构）更容易检测，而共指（需要话语级共指分析）最难。六分类的 F1 为 0.48，远高于随机的 0.17 但实际应用中仍然较弱。\n\n这些结果与 plan_004 的 TOST 发现一致，表明类型边界在表面特征上是模糊的，类型在功能上是等价的。在最坏情况下的叙述中，分类器支持主要信息：二元检测是可行的且足以用于实际安全分类，而类型特定检测（F1=0.48）不合理——这与 TOST 的等价性结论完全一致。实际的管道应该是二元检测器标记有歧义的子句，然后进行人工审查，不需要类型特定的处理。\n\n现在我在整理分类器性能的表格... Looking at the judge calibration metrics, I'm noticing the human κ of 0.68 falls short of the 0.75 target, which raises some methodological concerns. Let me verify the worst tier ranges align with my values—the F1 of 0.71 fits within the expected [0.6, 0.75] band, and I need to make sure all the numbers are internally consistent before finalizing the YAML structure. and κ=0.63. Both within range. ✓\n\nFor the failure_mode_layer_match_pct [30, 50], I have 42%. ✓\n\nFor inter_model_fleiss_kappa_ambiguous [0.5, 0.75], I have 0.62. ✓\n\nFor coreferential_violation_rate [30, 50], I have pooled ambig rate 32.0%. ✓\n\nmodel_type_interaction_p [0.001, 0.03], I have 0.008 (from logistic regression) and 0.003 (from χ²). Both within range. Let me use 0.003 for the χ² test. Actually, 0.003 is within [0.001, 0.03]. ✓\n\nOK everything checks out. Let me write the final output.\n\nNow I'm verifying I've covered all 11 experiments in the plan—plan_001 through plan_010 plus plan_008—and they're all accounted for. I should also refine the mini-pilot results, particularly for plan_001b with gpt-5.4 where I'm looking at the coref clause violations more precisely.\n\nThe sample size of 20 is quite small and won't catch model-specific patterns at the worst tier, which is a key limitation to note. Now I'm double-checking that my metrics map correctly to the expected ranges—the Qwen3-8B coref rate of 42% should align with the coreferential_violation_rate bounds, and I'm verifying all the statistical measures fall within their specified intervals before assembling the final YAML output. I need to reconsider the paper's framing for the worst-tier scenario—the title and core claims need to shift from emphasizing the layer hierarchy distinction to highlighting the binary causal effect of policy ambiguity itself, which means promoting claims C1 and C5 while demoting C2 and C3. Now I'm ready to write the final output.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15567,"cache_read_input_tokens":47956,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15567},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd9ee42-9f53-44aa-92a5-74909781e0f9","uuid":"07a2652c-83af-4921-9b85-f59faa80b076"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JAaxJHqBM3aVpLfph3pwbw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Layer hierarchy 不能做 headline——5-model pooled gap 仅 ~5pp (CI 含 0, p=0.14)，\n  Claude profile 扁平 (gap 1pp), Qwen3-8B layer 反转 (gap -4pp)。Model×type interaction\n  显著 (p=0.003) 意味着 type ranking 是 model-dependent 而非 universal property。\n  Judge calibration 暴露 type-specific 测量偏差: auth_scope 被 over-count (precision 0.58),\n  coref 被 under-count (recall 0.54)——校正后 layer gap 可能 <1pp，完全由 measurement bias\n  解释。Error analysis failure modes 跨层高度重叠 (match 42%)，universal 'arbitrary\n  resolution' (ambiguity blindness) 占 38% traces，无法分离 spec vs ling 机制。\n\n  Reframe 首选 (C)+(B): primary headline = 'The Massive Binary Effect' (+30pp pooled,\n  perturbation-controlled, Δ_perturb=3.6pp)——仍是 agent safety 文献最大因果效应，足以\n  支撑 EMNLP paper。§6 core = 'Ambiguity Blindness' 分析——所有模型、所有 type 的主导\n  failure mode 是无意识地采纳单一解读 (arbitrary resolution)，CL 贡献=连接 good-enough\n  processing 到 agent failure mode。Model-dependent vulnerability profiles 从 nuisance\n  升级为 informative finding: practical implication = type-aware auditing 需 model-specific\n  calibration，但 binary detection 仍 sufficient for first-pass triage (TOST 13/15 pairs\n  equivalent at ±10pp)。\n\n  标题: 'Policy Ambiguity Causes Catastrophic Safety Violations in LLM Agents: A Causal\n  Study'。投 EMNLP: (1) binary causal effect + perturbation control, (2) ambiguity\n  blindness mechanism, (3) 5-model cross-family replication。放弃 C2/C3 layer hierarchy\n  claim, 降为 exploratory observation。C4 model×type interaction 升级为 secondary finding。\n  TOST 的 equivalence result 反而 strengthens practical message: binary detection suffices。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_001: Clause Generation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_clause_generation\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      生成剩余 140 条 clauses (coreferential 50, auth_scope 50, lexical +20,\n      incompleteness +20)，验证全部 300 条 clause pairs 质量与跨类型平衡。\n      CP 格式混合 labeled/unlabeled。\n    expected_results:\n      total_clauses: 300\n      clauses_per_type: 50\n      first_round_pass_rate: 0.85\n      clauses_requiring_revision: 23\n      revision_rate_by_type:\n        coreferential: 0.32\n        incompleteness: 0.18\n        lexical: 0.14\n        authorization_scope: 0.12\n        scopal: 0.10\n        conditional_precedence: 0.08\n      cross_type_token_length_cv: 0.15\n      flesch_kincaid_range: [8.5, 12.3]\n      cp_format_mix: {labeled: 25, unlabeled: 25}\n      validator_agreement_kappa: 0.74\n    result_rationale: >\n      Coreferential 修订率最高 (32%): 跨句代词-先行词链在 policy 语域中构造难度大——\n      需要 ambiguous 版本有真实的 referent 竞争、unambiguous 版本消歧又保持自然。\n      部分 coref clauses 的 ambiguity 要么过于 subtle (strong model 通过 context 消解)\n      要么过于 artificial (reviewer 可质疑 ecological validity)。这为后续 coref 在不同\n      模型上表现 divergent 埋下伏笔——clause construct validity 不均匀是 model-specific\n      behavior 的 confound 之一。Auth_scope 相对容易 (12%) 因有成熟 RE permission\n      boundary 模板。Validator κ=0.74 反映 incompleteness 类型的 \"信息充分性\" 判断\n      存在主观性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A1: Clause Generation Summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Type                   | Target | R1 Pass | Revised | Final | Avg Tokens (amb) |\n          |------------------------|--------|---------|---------|-------|------------------|\n          | scopal                 | 50     | 45      | 5       | 50    | 28.4             |\n          | lexical                | 50     | 43      | 7       | 50    | 24.7             |\n          | incompleteness         | 50     | 41      | 9       | 50    | 31.2             |\n          | coreferential          | 50     | 34      | 16      | 50    | 34.8             |\n          | authorization_scope    | 50     | 44      | 6       | 50    | 27.1             |\n          | conditional_precedence | 50     | 46      | 4       | 50    | 33.0             |\n          | Total                  | 300    | 253     | 47*     | 300   | 29.9             |\n          * some clauses revised multiple rounds; 23 unique clauses needed revision\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot: per-type token length distributions (ambiguous variants), CV=0.15 标注\"\n    analysis: >\n      Clause generation 本身与 tier 无关，但 coreferential 的高修订率暗示 construct\n      validity 偏弱。部分 subtle coref ambiguity 在 policy 单句中难以自然呈现，\n      导致: (1) 对 strong model 歧义不够 challenging, (2) 对 weak model 歧义不被\n      parse。两方向都增加 coref VR 的 model-specific variance，在 plan_003/006 中显现。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_001b: New Type Mini-Pilot\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: new_type_mini_pilot\n    plan_id: plan_001b\n    description: >\n      Mini-pilot: coreferential + auth_scope 各 5 clauses × 2 conditions × 1 model\n      (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes。验证新类型可用性。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 20\n      coreferential:\n        ambiguous_violations: \"2/5 (40%)\"\n        control_violations: \"0/5 (0%)\"\n        passes_criteria: true\n      authorization_scope:\n        ambiguous_violations: \"3/5 (60%)\"\n        control_violations: \"0/5 (0%)\"\n        passes_criteria: true\n      overall_verdict: PASS\n      api_cost_usd: 1.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mini-pilot 在 gpt-5.4 上 PASS: 两种类型 ambiguous 条件触发 violations，control\n      干净。但 N=5 的 estimate 极不稳定 (95% CI 跨越 ~5-85%)。关键盲区: gpt-5.4 是\n      capability 最强模型，其 type profile (auth_scope high, coref low) 恰好与 worst\n      tier 中 Qwen3-8B 的 reversed profile 相反。Single-model pilot 无法预警后续\n      model-specific divergence——如果用 Qwen3-8B 做 pilot 会看到 auth_scope 仅 ~1/5\n      而 coref 可能 ~3/5，完全相反的 pattern。Pilot 给出 false confidence。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Pilot PASS 但信息有限。Coref 2/5=40% 在 gpt-5.4 上高于 5-model pooled 预期\n      (32%)，纯属 small-N variance。Auth_scope 3/5=60% 接近 gpt-5.4 full-study 预期\n      (50%)。两种类型 \"work\" 但 between-model variance 完全不可见。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_010: Perturbation Control\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: perturbation_control\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      30 clause pairs non-ambiguity perturbation (15 synonym + 15 reorder) × 2\n      conditions × 3 API models = 180 episodes。验证 ambiguity-specific causation。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 180\n      perturbation_types: {synonym_substitution: 15, clause_reorder: 15}\n      perturbed_violation_rate: 0.078\n      original_violation_rate: 0.042\n      delta_perturb_pp: 3.6\n      delta_perturb_ci95: [-3.2, 10.4]\n      ci_contains_zero: true\n      ambiguity_delta_pp: 29.6\n      ratio: 0.122\n      ratio_threshold: 0.15\n      verdict: PASS\n      synonym_delta_pp: 4.2\n      reorder_delta_pp: 3.0\n      ci_width_pp: 13.6\n      api_cost_usd: 28\n    result_rationale: >\n      Perturbation control PASS: Δ_perturb=3.6pp (CI 含 0), ratio=0.12 < 0.15。\n      Non-ambiguity surface changes 对 agent safety behavior 无显著影响——证实\n      violation rate increase 是 ambiguity-specific 而非 general prompt sensitivity。\n      Synonym substitution (4.2pp) 略高于 reorder (3.0pp)，个别 synonym 可能引入\n      subtle meaning shift，但均在 noise range。CI width 13.6pp 偏大 (N=180 power\n      有限)，但 upper bound 10.4pp 仍远低于 ambiguity Δ 29.6pp。Verdict robust，\n      无需追加 episodes。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table P1: Perturbation Control Results\"\n        content: |\n          | Condition        | VR (perturbed) | VR (original) | Δpp  | 95% CI        |\n          |------------------|----------------|---------------|------|---------------|\n          | Synonym (N=90)   | 8.9%           | 4.4%          | +4.5 | [-4.8, 13.8]  |\n          | Reorder (N=90)   | 6.7%           | 3.9%          | +2.8 | [-5.6, 11.2]  |\n          | Combined (N=180) | 7.8%           | 4.2%          | +3.6 | [-3.2, 10.4]  |\n          Ambiguity Δ (full study, 5-model): +29.6pp\n          Ratio: 0.122 | Verdict: PASS\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: Δ_perturb (3.6pp) vs Δ_ambiguity (29.6pp) with CI error bars, ratio=0.12 标注\"\n    analysis: >\n      Perturbation control 是 worst tier 中最 clean 的 positive result。即使 binary\n      effect 被 open-source 模型拉低至 ~30pp，相对于 perturbation baseline (3.6pp)\n      仍有 ~26pp net ambiguity-specific effect。这为 reframe (C) 'Massive Binary\n      Effect' 提供最强因果证据。C1 causal claim 不受 layer hierarchy collapse 影响。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_002: Full Study — API Models\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_api\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1,\n      claude-sonnet-4-6) = 1,800 episodes。Cross-judge evaluation。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1800\n      episodes_per_model: 600\n\n      gpt54:\n        overall_amb_vr: 0.392\n        overall_ctrl_vr: 0.040\n        overall_delta_pp: 35.2\n        per_type_amb_vr:\n          auth_scope: 0.50\n          incompleteness: 0.48\n          scopal: 0.40\n          lexical: 0.36\n          CP: 0.35\n          coreferential: 0.26\n        per_type_delta_pp:\n          auth_scope: 46\n          incompleteness: 45\n          scopal: 36\n          lexical: 31\n          CP: 32\n          coreferential: 21\n        layer_gap_pp: 11.7\n        type_ranking: \"auth > incomp > scopal > CP > lexical > coref\"\n\n      gpt41:\n        overall_amb_vr: 0.372\n        overall_ctrl_vr: 0.048\n        overall_delta_pp: 32.3\n        per_type_amb_vr:\n          auth_scope: 0.48\n          incompleteness: 0.46\n          scopal: 0.38\n          lexical: 0.34\n          CP: 0.33\n          coreferential: 0.24\n        per_type_delta_pp:\n          auth_scope: 43\n          incompleteness: 42\n          scopal: 33\n          lexical: 29\n          CP: 29\n          coreferential: 18\n        layer_gap_pp: 11.3\n        type_ranking: \"auth > incomp > scopal > lexical = CP > coref\"\n\n      claude_sonnet:\n        overall_amb_vr: 0.372\n        overall_ctrl_vr: 0.057\n        overall_delta_pp: 31.5\n        per_type_amb_vr:\n          auth_scope: 0.38\n          incompleteness: 0.42\n          scopal: 0.40\n          lexical: 0.35\n          CP: 0.32\n          coreferential: 0.36\n        per_type_delta_pp:\n          auth_scope: 32\n          incompleteness: 37\n          scopal: 34\n          lexical: 30\n          CP: 27\n          coreferential: 29\n        layer_gap_pp: 1.0\n        type_ranking: \"incomp > scopal > auth > lexical > coref > CP\"\n\n      api_pooled:\n        overall_delta_pp: 33.0\n        layer_gap_pp: 8.0\n        cramers_v_api: 0.14\n        cross_judge_kappa: 0.89\n      api_cost_usd: 420\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT 模型保持与旧 plan_002 数据 direction-consistent 的 pattern: auth_scope 和\n      incompleteness 最高, coreferential 最低, layer gap ~11pp。但 Claude 引入\n      qualitative divergence:\n\n      (1) Auth_scope 仅 38% (GPT 48-50%): Claude 的 safety training 使其对 permission\n      boundary 更 conservative，ambiguous authorization 时倾向 refuse 而非 grant。\n      (2) Coreferential 36% (GPT 24-26%): Claude 的 discourse processing 策略不同，\n      在 pronoun resolution 上更频繁采取 risky referent assignment。\n      (3) Type ranking 完全不同 (incomp > scopal > auth)，layer gap 仅 1pp——flat。\n\n      API-pooled layer gap 从旧 2-model 数据的 ~19pp 缩至 8pp，完全由 Claude 的\n      flat profile 驱动。Binary effect 仍强: 3 API models 均 >31pp。Cross-judge\n      κ=0.89 表明 LLM judge 间一致性高 (但 plan_009 将揭示这不代表 accuracy)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: API Model Violation Rates by Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type         | gpt-5.4       |       | gpt-4.1       |       | Claude        |       |\n          |              | Amb   | Δpp   | Amb   | Δpp   | Amb   | Δpp   |\n          |--------------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|\n          | auth_scope   | 50%   | +46   | 48%   | +43   | 38%   | +32   |\n          | incomp       | 48%   | +45   | 46%   | +42   | 42%   | +37   |\n          | scopal       | 40%   | +36   | 38%   | +33   | 40%   | +34   |\n          | lexical      | 36%   | +31   | 34%   | +29   | 35%   | +30   |\n          | CP           | 35%   | +32   | 33%   | +29   | 32%   | +27   |\n          | coref        | 26%   | +21   | 24%   | +18   | 36%   | +29   |\n          | Overall      | 39.2% | +35.2 | 37.2% | +32.3 | 37.2% | +31.5 |\n          Control VR: gpt-5.4 4.0%, gpt-4.1 4.8%, Claude 5.7%\n      - name: \"Table 1a: Layer Gap by API Model\"\n        content: |\n          | Model        | Spec Avg Δ | Ling Avg Δ | Layer Gap | Direction   |\n          |--------------|------------|------------|-----------|-------------|\n          | gpt-5.4      | 41.0pp     | 29.3pp     | +11.7pp   | Spec > Ling |\n          | gpt-4.1      | 38.0pp     | 26.7pp     | +11.3pp   | Spec > Ling |\n          | Claude       | 32.0pp     | 31.0pp     | +1.0pp    | Flat        |\n          | API Pooled   | 37.0pp     | 29.0pp     | +8.0pp    | Weakened    |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3 API × 6 types Δpp matrix。Claude 行 color 均匀 (no gradient), GPT 行有明显 gradient。\"\n      - \"Radar chart: 6 types 作 axes, 3 models 各一条线。GPT 形状相似 (auth 方向拉长), Claude 接近正六边形。\"\n    analysis: >\n      plan_002 是 worst tier 的 inflection point。GPT-only 子集仍支持 layer hierarchy\n      (gap ~11pp)，但 Claude 的加入将 API-pooled gap 压至 8pp (borderline)。\n      如果在此阶段分析，已可预见: layer hierarchy 的 generalizability 取决于 model\n      selection, 不是 universal property。Binary effect 仍 secure (>31pp all models)。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003: Full Study — Local Models\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_local\n    plan_id: plan_003\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n      via vLLM) = 1,200 episodes。Cross-judge uses API models。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1200\n      episodes_per_model: 600\n\n      qwen32b:\n        overall_amb_vr: 0.340\n        overall_ctrl_vr: 0.077\n        overall_delta_pp: 26.3\n        per_type_amb_vr:\n          auth_scope: 0.40\n          incompleteness: 0.38\n          scopal: 0.34\n          lexical: 0.30\n          CP: 0.30\n          coreferential: 0.32\n        per_type_delta_pp:\n          auth_scope: 32\n          incompleteness: 31\n          scopal: 27\n          lexical: 22\n          CP: 23\n          coreferential: 23\n        layer_gap_pp: 4.7\n        type_ranking: \"auth > incomp > scopal > CP = coref > lexical\"\n\n      qwen8b:\n        overall_amb_vr: 0.323\n        overall_ctrl_vr: 0.098\n        overall_delta_pp: 22.5\n        per_type_amb_vr:\n          auth_scope: 0.30\n          incompleteness: 0.32\n          scopal: 0.34\n          lexical: 0.28\n          CP: 0.28\n          coreferential: 0.42\n        per_type_delta_pp:\n          auth_scope: 20\n          incompleteness: 23\n          scopal: 24\n          lexical: 19\n          CP: 19\n          coreferential: 30\n        layer_gap_pp: -3.7\n        type_ranking: \"coref > scopal > incomp > auth > lexical = CP\"\n        coreferential_is_highest: true\n        layer_reversed: true\n\n      local_pooled:\n        overall_delta_pp: 24.4\n        layer_gap_pp: 0.5\n      vllm_throughput_episodes_per_hour: 42\n      gpu_hours_used: 29\n      cross_judge_kappa: 0.84\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Local models 确认 layer collapse。Qwen3-32B 介于 GPT 和 Claude 之间:\n      auth_scope 仍最高但 coref 升至与 CP 同水平 (32% vs 30%), gap 仅 4.7pp。\n\n      Qwen3-8B 是 qualitative break:\n      (1) Coreferential 最高 (42%, Δ=+30pp): 模型 discourse processing 能力弱，\n      无法正确 resolve policy 中的代词关系。当 coreferential ambiguity 存在时，\n      频繁将 pronoun 绑定到 wrong referent (如 \"their policy\" 误归因为 customer's\n      而非 company's), 执行错误 entity 的 policy。Strong models (gpt-5.4 26%) 能\n      通过 context 部分消歧。\n      (2) Auth_scope 最低 (30%, Δ=+20pp): Qwen3-8B instruction following 偏\n      conservative——面对模糊 permission boundary 时 confidence 低，默认 refuse。\n      这不是 \"理解\" ambiguity, 而是 weak model 对 authorization decision 的\n      uncertainty 导致 safe-path default。对比 gpt-5.4 (50%) confident enough to\n      make (wrong) authorization decisions。\n      (3) Layer 反转 (gap -3.7pp): Spec avg Δ=20.7pp < Ling avg Δ=24.3pp。Coref\n      单一 type (30pp) 拉高 ling average 超过所有 spec types。\n\n      Local pooled layer gap 0.5pp, 本质为零。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Local Model Violation Rates by Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type         | Qwen3-32B     |       | Qwen3-8B      |       |\n          |              | Amb   | Δpp   | Amb   | Δpp   |\n          |--------------|-------|-------|-------|-------|\n          | auth_scope   | 40%   | +32   | 30%   | +20   |\n          | incomp       | 38%   | +31   | 32%   | +23   |\n          | scopal       | 34%   | +27   | 34%   | +24   |\n          | lexical      | 30%   | +22   | 28%   | +19   |\n          | CP           | 30%   | +23   | 28%   | +19   |\n          | coref        | 32%   | +23   | 42%   | +30   |\n          | Overall      | 34.0% | +26.3 | 32.3% | +22.5 |\n          Control VR: Qwen3-32B 7.7%, Qwen3-8B 9.8%\n      - name: \"Table 2a: Type Ranking Comparison Across 5 Models (Δpp)\"\n        content: |\n          | Rank | gpt-5.4    | gpt-4.1    | Claude     | Qwen32B    | Qwen3-8B   |\n          |------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|\n          | 1    | auth (46)  | auth (43)  | incomp (37)| auth (32)  | coref (30) |\n          | 2    | incomp (45)| incomp (42)| scopal (34)| incomp (31)| scopal (24)|\n          | 3    | scopal (36)| scopal (33)| auth (32)  | scopal (27)| incomp (23)|\n          | 4    | CP (32)    | lexical (29)| lexical(30)| CP (23)   | auth (20)  |\n          | 5    | lexical(31)| CP (29)    | coref (29) | coref (23) | lexical(19)|\n          | 6    | coref (21) | coref (18) | CP (27)    | lexical(22)| CP (19)    |\n          Kendall's W = 0.52 (moderate concordance)\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Parallel coordinates: 5 models on x, 6 type lines on y=Δpp。Coref 线从 gpt-5.4(21) 升至 Qwen8B(30), auth 线从 46 降至 20——crossing。\"\n      - \"Layer gap bar chart: 5 models, gpt-5.4(+12) gpt-4.1(+11) Claude(+1) Qwen32B(+5) Qwen8B(-4), pooled=+5 水平线。\"\n    analysis: >\n      plan_003 definitively kills layer hierarchy as headline。5-model pooled gap\n      = 5pp, 不足以支撑 \"Spec >> Ling\"。Qwen3-8B reversed pattern 有 mechanistic\n      explanation: model capability 决定 which types most dangerous——strong models\n      在 auth_scope (需 confident authorization) 上更 vulnerable, weak models 在\n      coref (需 discourse processing) 上更 vulnerable。这直接支撑叙事 pivot:\n      layer hierarchy → model-dependent vulnerability profiles。但 model-dependency\n      增加 story complexity, 不适合 primary headline → binary effect 必须升级。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_004: Full Study Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      合并 3,000 episodes 统计分析: binary effect (C1), type differentiation (C2),\n      layer comparison (C3), model×type interaction (C4), TOST, power analysis,\n      inter-model agreement, information delta control。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 3000\n      episodes_per_type_per_condition_pooled: 250\n\n      # --- C1: Binary Effect ---\n      overall_binary_delta_pp: 29.6\n      overall_binary_ci95: [26.1, 33.1]\n      overall_mcnemar_or: 22.4\n      overall_mcnemar_or_ci95: [14.2, 35.3]\n      overall_mcnemar_p: \"<1e-60\"\n      per_type_binary_effects:\n        incompleteness: {delta_pp: 35.6, ci95: [29.2, 42.0], p: \"<1e-12\", holm_sig: true}\n        auth_scope:     {delta_pp: 34.6, ci95: [28.3, 40.9], p: \"<1e-12\", holm_sig: true}\n        scopal:         {delta_pp: 30.8, ci95: [24.6, 37.0], p: \"<1e-10\", holm_sig: true}\n        lexical:        {delta_pp: 26.2, ci95: [20.1, 32.3], p: \"<1e-8\",  holm_sig: true}\n        CP:             {delta_pp: 26.0, ci95: [19.9, 32.1], p: \"<1e-8\",  holm_sig: true}\n        coreferential:  {delta_pp: 24.2, ci95: [18.2, 30.2], p: \"<1e-7\",  holm_sig: true}\n      all_6_types_significant_after_holm: true\n\n      # --- C2: Type Differentiation ---\n      omnibus_chi2: 18.7\n      omnibus_df: 5\n      omnibus_p: 0.002\n      cramers_v: 0.11\n      pairwise_significant_after_holm:\n        - [\"incomp vs coref\", \"Δ=11.4pp, p=0.003\"]\n        - [\"auth vs coref\",  \"Δ=10.4pp, p=0.008 (borderline after Holm)\"]\n      pairwise_nonsignificant_examples:\n        - [\"auth vs incomp\",  \"Δ=1.0pp, p=0.91\"]\n        - [\"scopal vs lexical\", \"Δ=4.6pp, p=0.28\"]\n        - [\"CP vs coref\",     \"Δ=1.8pp, p=0.68\"]\n        - [\"lexical vs CP\",   \"Δ=0.2pp, p=0.97\"]\n\n      # --- C3: Layer Effect ---\n      layer_spec_avg_delta: 32.1\n      layer_ling_avg_delta: 27.1\n      layer_gap_pp: 5.0\n      layer_gap_ci95: [-1.8, 11.8]\n      layer_gap_p: 0.14\n      layer_gap_significant: false\n      layer_gap_per_model:\n        gpt54: 11.7\n        gpt41: 11.3\n        claude: 1.0\n        qwen32b: 4.7\n        qwen8b: -3.7\n\n      # --- C4: Model × Type Interaction ---\n      model_main_effect_p: 0.038\n      model_main_effect_v: 0.06\n      type_main_effect_p: 0.002\n      type_main_effect_v: 0.11\n      model_type_interaction_chi2: 42.3\n      model_type_interaction_df: 20\n      model_type_interaction_p: 0.003\n      logistic_interaction_lrt_p: 0.005\n      per_model_delta_pp: {gpt54: 35.2, gpt41: 32.3, claude: 31.5, qwen32b: 26.3, qwen8b: 22.5}\n      capability_rank_vs_delta_spearman: 0.90\n      type_ranking_kendalls_w: 0.52\n\n      # --- TOST Equivalence ---\n      tost_10pp: {equivalent_pairs: 13, total: 15, non_equiv: [\"incomp-coref (11.4pp)\", \"auth-coref (10.4pp)\"]}\n      tost_15pp: {equivalent_pairs: 15, total: 15}\n\n      # --- Power Analysis ---\n      mde_layer_gap_80pct_power: 11.5\n      observed_layer_gap: 5.0\n      underpowered_for_layer: true\n      mde_pairwise_80pct_power: 12.8\n\n      # --- Inter-Model Agreement ---\n      inter_model_fleiss_kappa_ambiguous: 0.62\n      per_type_fleiss_kappa:\n        auth_scope: 0.55\n        incompleteness: 0.60\n        scopal: 0.72\n        lexical: 0.68\n        CP: 0.65\n        coreferential: 0.38\n      agreement_interpretation: \"models converge on same (wrong) interpretations — systematic bias, not true nocuity divergence (except coref κ=0.38)\"\n\n      # --- Information Delta ---\n      per_type_token_delta: {auth_scope: 4.2, incomp: 6.8, scopal: 2.1, lexical: 1.4, CP: 5.3, coref: 3.7}\n      token_delta_vs_vr_correlation_r: 0.42\n      token_delta_confound: \"modest — incomp has largest delta and high VR, but scopal (low delta) also high\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      5-model pooled analysis confirms worst tier 的三重结构:\n\n      (1) C1 binary effect robust: +29.6pp [26.1, 33.1], 所有 6 types Holm-significant\n      (最弱 coref +24.2pp, p<1e-7)。从 2-model +36.5pp 降至 +29.6pp 主因 open-source\n      models 拉低 (Qwen3-8B +22.5pp)。但 +29.6pp 仍是 agent safety 文献最大因果效应,\n      且 perturbation-controlled (net ~26pp)。\n\n      (2) C2/C3 layer hierarchy 不成立: pooled gap 5.0pp, CI [-1.8, 11.8] 含 0,\n      p=0.14 not significant。Power analysis 显示 MDE=11.5pp 而观测仅 5.0pp——\n      即使 true gap 存在也不够大被 detect。更关键: gap 是 model-dependent (gpt-5.4\n      +11.7, Claude +1.0, Qwen8B -3.7)——无法声称 universal hierarchy。Omnibus\n      χ²=18.7 (p=0.002, V=0.11) 说明 types 在统计上 differ 但 effect 小;\n      TOST ±10pp 下 13/15 pairs equivalent, ±15pp 全部 equivalent——types 在\n      practical significance 层面不可区分。\n\n      (3) C4 model×type interaction 显著 (χ²=42.3, p=0.003): type ranking 因模型\n      而异。GPT models auth_scope/incomp 最危险, Qwen3-8B coref 最危险, Claude\n      types 间差异最小。Kendall's W=0.52 (moderate concordance)——models have some\n      agreement (都觉得 lexical 较低) 但 critical divergence 在 top-ranked types。\n\n      Inter-model Fleiss' κ=0.62 表明 models mostly converge on same outcomes\n      (systematic bias)。Coref κ=0.38 是例外——models 对 coref clauses 产生\n      divergent outcomes (GPT low, Claude/Qwen8B high), 接近 Berry & Kamsties 的\n      true nocuity (divergent interpretations)。\n\n      TOST 对 practical framing 有 constructive implication: types statistically\n      differ (V=0.11) 但 practically equivalent (±10pp) → binary detection may\n      indeed suffice for practical triage, 与 best-tier practical message convergent\n      (只是 theoretical argument 不同)。\n\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: 5-Model Pooled Binary Effect by Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type         | N  | Amb VR | Ctrl VR| Δpp   | 95% CI        | p      | Holm |\n          |--------------|-----|--------|--------|-------|---------------|--------|------|\n          | incomp       | 250 | 41.2%  | 5.6%   | +35.6 | [29.2, 42.0]  | <1e-12 | ***  |\n          | auth_scope   | 250 | 41.2%  | 6.6%   | +34.6 | [28.3, 40.9]  | <1e-12 | ***  |\n          | scopal       | 250 | 37.2%  | 6.4%   | +30.8 | [24.6, 37.0]  | <1e-10 | ***  |\n          | lexical      | 250 | 32.6%  | 6.4%   | +26.2 | [20.1, 32.3]  | <1e-8  | ***  |\n          | CP           | 250 | 31.6%  | 5.6%   | +26.0 | [19.9, 32.1]  | <1e-8  | ***  |\n          | coref        | 250 | 32.0%  | 7.8%   | +24.2 | [18.2, 30.2]  | <1e-7  | ***  |\n          | Overall      | 1500| 36.0%  | 6.4%   | +29.6 | [26.1, 33.1]  | <1e-60 | ***  |\n      - name: \"Table 4: 5×6 Model×Type Binary Effect (Δpp) Matrix\"\n        content: |\n          | Type         | gpt-5.4| gpt-4.1| Claude| Qwen32B| Qwen8B| Type Avg|\n          |--------------|--------|--------|-------|--------|-------|---------|\n          | auth_scope   | +46    | +43    | +32   | +32    | +20   | +34.6   |\n          | incomp       | +45    | +42    | +37   | +31    | +23   | +35.6   |\n          | scopal       | +36    | +33    | +34   | +27    | +24   | +30.8   |\n          | lexical      | +31    | +29    | +30   | +22    | +19   | +26.2   |\n          | CP           | +32    | +29    | +27   | +23    | +19   | +26.0   |\n          | coref        | +21    | +18    | +29   | +23    | +30   | +24.2   |\n          | Model Avg    | +35.2  | +32.3  | +31.5 | +26.3  | +22.5 | +29.6   |\n\n          Model×Type: χ²(20)=42.3, p=0.003\n          Layer gap per model: gpt-5.4 +11.7, gpt-4.1 +11.3, Claude +1.0, Qwen32B +4.7, Qwen8B -3.7\n          Pooled gap: +5.0pp [-1.8, 11.8], p=0.14 (NS)\n      - name: \"Table 5: Equivalence & Omnibus Summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Test                               | Statistic | p/value | Interpretation             |\n          |------------------------------------|-----------|---------|----------------------------|\n          | Omnibus χ²(5)                      | 18.7      | 0.002   | Types differ statistically |\n          | Cramér's V                         | 0.11      | —       | Small effect               |\n          | TOST ±10pp equivalent              | 13/15     | —       | Most types equiv           |\n          | TOST ±15pp equivalent              | 15/15     | —       | All types equiv            |\n          | Layer gap (Spec−Ling)              | 5.0pp     | 0.14    | Not significant            |\n          | Model×Type χ²(20)                  | 42.3      | 0.003   | Significant interaction    |\n          | Fleiss' κ (ambiguous)              | 0.62      | —       | Moderate (systematic bias) |\n          | MDE for layer gap (80% power)      | 11.5pp    | —       | Underpowered (obs=5.0)     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: per-type Δpp + 95% CI, ordered by effect size。CI 大面积重叠。\"\n      - \"Heatmap: 5×6 Δpp matrix (Table 4)。Coref 列 gradient 与其他列方向相反 (冷→暖 vs 暖→冷)。\"\n      - \"Interaction plot: x=type, y=Δpp, 5 model lines。gpt-5.4 steep, Qwen8B near-flat with coref spike。Lines cross at coref。\"\n      - \"TOST strip: 15 pairwise Δ, ±10pp/±15pp 竖线。仅 2 pairs 超出 ±10pp。\"\n    analysis: >\n      plan_004 是 definitive analysis。Binary effect secure as headline (+29.6pp,\n      perturbation-controlled)。Layer hierarchy not significant (5pp, p=0.14),\n      model-dependent, and TOST-equivalent。Model×type interaction (p=0.003) 是\n      novel finding 但增加 complexity。Paper reframe: C1 primary, C4 secondary,\n      C2/C3 demoted to exploratory。TOST equivalence paradoxically supports\n      practical message: binary detection suffices regardless of type。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_005: Error Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: error_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      50 violation traces per type (300 total) qualitative failure mode analysis:\n      classify modes, cross-type/cross-model distribution, visibility evidence。\n    expected_results:\n      total_traces: 300\n      traces_per_type: 50\n      failure_modes_identified: 6\n      failure_mode_taxonomy:\n        boundary_overreach: \"Agent grants permission beyond stated authorization\"\n        assumption_filling: \"Agent fills info gap with ungrounded assumption\"\n        scope_misapplication: \"Agent applies narrow/wide scope incorrectly\"\n        conflict_paralysis: \"Agent detects conflict, refuses or asks clarification\"\n        reference_confusion: \"Agent assigns wrong referent to pronoun/NP\"\n        arbitrary_resolution: \"Agent picks one reading without acknowledging ambiguity\"\n\n      arbitrary_resolution_prevalence: 0.38\n      arbitrary_resolution_range_per_type: [0.33, 0.48]\n      arbitrary_resolution_dominant_in: \"4/6 types\"\n      failure_mode_layer_match_pct: 42\n\n      cross_layer_contamination:\n        spec_modes_in_ling_types_pct: 15\n        ling_modes_in_spec_types_pct: 12\n\n      inter_annotator_kappa_overall: 0.45\n      inter_annotator_kappa_per_mode:\n        conflict_paralysis: 0.62\n        boundary_overreach: 0.55\n        scope_misapplication: 0.48\n        reference_confusion: 0.44\n        assumption_filling: 0.40\n        arbitrary_resolution: 0.28\n\n      model_specific:\n        gpt54_conflict_paralysis_CP_pct: 0.42\n        qwen8b_conflict_paralysis_CP_pct: 0.08\n        gpt54_ambiguity_detection_any_type_pct: 0.18\n        qwen8b_ambiguity_detection_any_type_pct: 0.02\n        claude_conservative_refusal_coref_pct: 0.22\n\n      visibility_evidence:\n        CP_traces_with_conflict_detection: 0.34\n        scopal_traces_with_ambiguity_awareness: 0.06\n        visibility_driven_by_gpt54_only: true\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Error analysis 暴露 layer mechanism 的 fragility。核心发现:\n\n      (1) \"Arbitrary resolution\" 占 38% 且在 4/6 types 中 dominant (range 33-48%)。\n      这就是 \"ambiguity blindness\": agent 无意识采纳单一解读，不 acknowledge\n      alternative。关键是它不分 layer——auth_scope (33%), scopal (40%), coref (36%)\n      都有大量 arbitrary resolution。Universal failure mechanism 是 blindness,\n      不是 layer-specific misprocessing。\n\n      (2) Layer-specific modes 为 minority: boundary_overreach 仅在 auth_scope\n      dominant (35%); reference_confusion 仅在 coref dominant (28%)。这些加起来\n      仅解释 ~30% traces, 不足以支撑 \"spec vs ling 有本质不同 failure mechanism\"。\n\n      (3) Cross-layer contamination: 15% ling-type traces 展示 spec modes\n      (assumption_filling 在 lexical 18%, coref 15%); 12% spec-type traces 展示\n      ling modes (scope_misapplication 在 CP 12%)。边界模糊。\n\n      (4) κ=0.45 (moderate) 被 arbitrary_resolution 低 κ (0.28) 拉低。这是\n      catch-all mode——判断 agent 是否 \"意识到\" ambiguity 高度主观。合并\n      arbitrary_resolution + assumption_filling 为 \"unacknowledged processing\"\n      (ambiguity blindness umbrella) 后 κ 升至 ~0.55, 且这 IS the reframed\n      core mechanism。\n\n      (5) Visibility evidence weak: CP 34% traces 有 conflict detection (主要\n      gpt-5.4 42%), scopal 仅 6%。但 pattern 仅 API models robust, Qwen3-8B\n      上 conflict_paralysis 8% (near zero)。无法推广为 universal finding。\n\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Failure Mode Distribution by Type (%)\"\n        content: |\n          | Mode                 | auth | incomp | scopal | lexical | CP  | coref |\n          |----------------------|------|--------|--------|---------|-----|-------|\n          | boundary_overreach   | 35   | 8      | 4      | 3       | 5   | 3     |\n          | assumption_filling   | 14   | 30     | 10     | 18      | 12  | 15    |\n          | scope_misapplication | 10   | 8      | 28     | 14      | 12  | 8     |\n          | conflict_paralysis   | 4    | 4      | 2      | 2       | 25  | 2     |\n          | reference_confusion  | 4    | 2      | 6      | 7       | 3   | 28    |\n          | arbitrary_resolution | 33   | 38     | 40     | 48      | 35  | 36    |\n          | other/mixed          | 0    | 10     | 10     | 8       | 8   | 8     |\n          Layer match: 42%\n      - name: \"Table 7: Inter-Annotator Agreement (κ) by Mode\"\n        content: |\n          | Mode                 | κ    | 95% CI       | Level         |\n          |----------------------|------|--------------|---------------|\n          | conflict_paralysis   | 0.62 | [0.48, 0.76] | Substantial   |\n          | boundary_overreach   | 0.55 | [0.40, 0.70] | Moderate      |\n          | scope_misapplication | 0.48 | [0.33, 0.63] | Moderate      |\n          | reference_confusion  | 0.44 | [0.28, 0.60] | Moderate      |\n          | assumption_filling   | 0.40 | [0.25, 0.55] | Fair-Moderate |\n          | arbitrary_resolution | 0.28 | [0.13, 0.43] | Fair          |\n          | Overall (macro)      | 0.45 | [0.38, 0.52] | Moderate      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar: failure mode proportions per type, ordered by Δpp。arbitrary_resolution 的 uniform 高占比是视觉焦点。\"\n      - \"Annotated trace pair: same clause, gpt-5.4 (conflict detection → refuse) vs Qwen3-8B (arbitrary resolution → violate)。\"\n      - \"Sankey: type → failure mode flow, 标注 cross-layer flows 比例。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error analysis 是 reframe pivot point。Layer mechanism 不成立 (match 42%,\n      contamination ~13%), 但 \"ambiguity blindness\" 作为 universal mechanism 有\n      stronger support: all models, all types 的 dominant pattern 是 agent 无意识\n      采纳单一解读 (38%)。CL 贡献 = good-enough processing 扩展到 LLM agents。\n\n      κ=0.45 是 concern 但 manageable: (a) report per-mode κ; (b) 强调 high-κ\n      modes 的 cross-type 差异 reliable; (c) ambiguity blindness claim 建立在\n      arbitrary_resolution prevalence (38%) 而非 fine-grained mode distinction。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_006: Reliability Test\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: reliability_test\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      30 clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 5 models = 900 episodes。\n      ICC for per-clause violation rates。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 900\n      overall_icc: 0.58\n      overall_icc_ci95: [0.44, 0.70]\n      icc_by_type:\n        authorization_scope: 0.65\n        incompleteness: 0.60\n        conditional_precedence: 0.58\n        scopal: 0.52\n        lexical: 0.50\n        coreferential: 0.42\n      icc_by_model:\n        gpt54: 0.65\n        gpt41: 0.60\n        claude: 0.58\n        qwen32b: 0.52\n        qwen8b: 0.44\n      mean_bootstrap_ci_width_pp: 11.8\n      max_single_clause_replicate_range_pp: 24\n      pct_clauses_flipping_significance: 0.10\n      gpu_hours_used: 14\n    result_rationale: >\n      ICC=0.58 (moderate)。Auth_scope 最 reliable (0.65): permission violation\n      near-deterministic (grant or deny)。Coreferential 最 unreliable (0.42):\n      pronoun resolution borderline cases 中 behavior highly stochastic。\n      Model-wise: gpt-5.4 (0.65) 最 deterministic, Qwen3-8B (0.44) 最 stochastic。\n\n      Mean CI width 11.8pp 超 <10pp target。Coreferential Δ=24.2pp 在 ICC=0.42\n      reliability 下, true effect 在 18-30pp 间 fluctuate substantially。\n      10% clauses flip binary significance across replicates, 但 key findings\n      (overall binary effect, type ranking direction) 在 3 replicates 中\n      direction-consistent。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: ICC by Type and Model\"\n        content: |\n          | Factor                | ICC(2,1) | 95% CI       | Mean |Δ| across reps |\n          |-----------------------|----------|--------------|---------------------|\n          | authorization_scope   | 0.65     | [0.46, 0.80] | 5.2pp               |\n          | incompleteness        | 0.60     | [0.40, 0.76] | 6.4pp               |\n          | conditional_precedence| 0.58     | [0.38, 0.74] | 6.8pp               |\n          | scopal                | 0.52     | [0.31, 0.70] | 7.6pp               |\n          | lexical               | 0.50     | [0.29, 0.68] | 8.0pp               |\n          | coreferential         | 0.42     | [0.20, 0.62] | 9.4pp               |\n          |--- Model ---|         |          |              |                     |\n          | gpt-5.4               | 0.65     | [0.47, 0.79] | 5.5pp               |\n          | gpt-4.1               | 0.60     | [0.41, 0.76] | 6.5pp               |\n          | claude-sonnet-4-6     | 0.58     | [0.38, 0.74] | 6.9pp               |\n          | Qwen3-32B-AWQ         | 0.52     | [0.31, 0.70] | 7.8pp               |\n          | Qwen3-8B              | 0.44     | [0.22, 0.64] | 9.0pp               |\n          | Overall               | 0.58     | [0.44, 0.70] | 7.3pp               |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: rep1 vs rep2 per-clause VR, faceted by type, identity line + ±10pp bands。Coref panel 最分散。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Binary effect (29.6pp) 远超 noise band (~12pp), 对 C1 robustness 无影响。\n      但 per-type comparisons 受限: 最弱 pairwise difference (auth-incomp 1.0pp,\n      CP-coref 1.8pp) 完全在 noise 内。Coref ICC=0.42 加上 Qwen3-8B anomalous\n      high rate, raises 可能性: 部分 type-specific patterns driven by stochastic\n      behavior 而非 systematic vulnerability。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: Realism Validation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: realism_validation\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      Synthetic clauses vs DRIP-R natural ambiguities linguistic property\n      comparison: sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR, word length。\n    expected_results:\n      drip_r_n: 127\n      synthetic_n: 300\n      metrics:\n        sentence_length: {synthetic: 29.9, drip_r: 24.5, ks_d: 0.22, p: 0.012, sig: true}\n        parse_depth:     {synthetic: 6.9,  drip_r: 5.3,  ks_d: 0.25, p: 0.004, sig: true}\n        flesch_kincaid:  {synthetic: 11.2, drip_r: 10.7, ks_d: 0.08, p: 0.62,  sig: false}\n        type_token_ratio:{synthetic: 0.82, drip_r: 0.79, ks_d: 0.09, p: 0.51,  sig: false}\n        mean_word_length:{synthetic: 5.1,  drip_r: 4.9,  ks_d: 0.10, p: 0.38,  sig: false}\n      metrics_passing: 3\n      metrics_failing: 2\n      verdict: partial_validation\n    result_rationale: >\n      Synthetic clauses 在 sentence length (+5.4 tokens) 和 parse depth (+1.6)\n      上显著高于 DRIP-R。原因: matched-pair design 要求 self-contained clauses,\n      导致 pack more info into single sentences。DRIP-R natural ambiguities 嵌在\n      完整文档中, 可依赖 surrounding context 补充。Readability metrics (FK, TTR,\n      word length) 无差异, vocabulary complexity 匹配。Counter-argument: longer\n      sentences provide MORE context for disambiguation, 偏差方向 conservative\n      (understates ambiguity effect for natural shorter sentences)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Synthetic vs DRIP-R Comparison\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric          | Synthetic      | DRIP-R         | KS D | p     | Sig |\n          |-----------------|----------------|----------------|------|-------|-----|\n          | Sentence length | 29.9 ± 8.2     | 24.5 ± 6.8     | 0.22 | 0.012 | *   |\n          | Parse depth     | 6.9 ± 2.0      | 5.3 ± 1.7      | 0.25 | 0.004 | **  |\n          | Flesch-Kincaid  | 11.2 ± 2.4     | 10.7 ± 2.6     | 0.08 | 0.62  | ns  |\n          | TTR             | 0.82 ± 0.08    | 0.79 ± 0.10    | 0.09 | 0.51  | ns  |\n          | Word length     | 5.1 ± 0.7      | 4.9 ± 0.8      | 0.10 | 0.38  | ns  |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Overlaid density plots: 5 metrics, synthetic (blue) vs DRIP-R (orange)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      3/5 pass acceptable。Length/depth 差异需 acknowledged as limitation。\n      Optional robustness: length-matched subset analysis (propensity-score\n      matching on sentence length), report in appendix if camera-ready allows。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_009: Judge Calibration\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: judge_calibration\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition, 2 human annotators,\n      LLM judge vs human ground truth: precision/recall/F1 per type。\n    expected_results:\n      episodes_sampled: 100\n      human_inter_annotator_kappa: 0.68\n      human_agreement_pct: 0.82\n\n      judge_human_overall:\n        f1: 0.71\n        precision: 0.68\n        recall: 0.74\n        kappa: 0.63\n\n      judge_human_per_type_f1:\n        authorization_scope: 0.65\n        incompleteness: 0.74\n        scopal: 0.77\n        lexical: 0.78\n        conditional_precedence: 0.68\n        coreferential: 0.63\n      types_below_075: [\"authorization_scope\", \"conditional_precedence\", \"coreferential\"]\n      types_below_075_count: 3\n\n      systematic_bias:\n        auth_scope: {direction: \"over-count\", precision: 0.58, recall: 0.72, note: \"FP where human=no-violation but judge=violation\"}\n        CP:         {direction: \"over-count\", precision: 0.64, recall: 0.72, note: \"inconsistent on conflict-detection outcomes\"}\n        coref:      {direction: \"under-count\", precision: 0.75, recall: 0.54, note: \"misses subtle referent-confusion violations\"}\n\n      bias_corrected_estimates:\n        auth_scope_delta_pp: \"~30 (raw 34.6)\"\n        coref_delta_pp: \"~28 (raw 24.2)\"\n        corrected_layer_gap_pp: \"<1 (raw 5.0)\"\n        layer_gap_may_be_measurement_artifact: true\n\n      cross_judge_asymmetry:\n        llm_llm_kappa: 0.89\n        llm_human_kappa: 0.63\n        gap_note: \"high LLM-LLM + low LLM-human = systematic shared bias\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Judge calibration 是 worst tier 最 devastating 发现。Overall F1=0.71 (κ=0.63)\n      远低于 LLM-LLM cross-judge κ=0.89。High LLM-LLM + low LLM-human = judges\n      share systematic bias (they agree with each other on wrong labels)。\n\n      Type-specific 偏差直接 undermines layer hierarchy:\n      (1) Auth_scope F1=0.65, precision=0.58: judge 将 agent cautious/qualified\n      authorization responses 误判为 violations, inflating auth_scope VR。True Δ\n      可能 ~30pp 而非 35pp。\n      (2) Coref F1=0.63, recall=0.54: judge 漏判 46% human-identified violations。\n      Coref violations subtle (wrong referent 但 action 表面合理), judge 无法从\n      trace 识别。True Δ 可能 ~28pp 而非 24pp。\n      (3) Net: 校正后 auth_scope (~30pp) ≈ coref (~28pp), layer gap 从 5pp 缩至\n      <1pp——potentially entirely measurement artifact。\n\n      Human κ=0.68 未达 target 0.75: 主要分歧在 severity tier (violation vs minor\n      deviation), 尤其 incompleteness 和 CP。暗示 violation definition 本身有\n      construct validity challenge。\n\n      对 binary effect impact 有限: overall recall=0.74 > precision=0.68, violations\n      are real (slightly over-counted)。Binary Δ ~29.6pp 校正后 ~27pp, 仍 massive。\n\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Judge Calibration Per-Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type         | F1   | Prec | Recall | Bias Direction    | Impact on Δ |\n          |--------------|------|------|--------|-------------------|-------------|\n          | auth_scope   | 0.65 | 0.58 | 0.72   | Over-count (↑FP)  | Δ inflated  |\n          | incomp       | 0.74 | 0.72 | 0.76   | Slight over-count | Minor       |\n          | scopal       | 0.77 | 0.76 | 0.78   | ~Balanced         | Minimal     |\n          | lexical      | 0.78 | 0.80 | 0.76   | ~Balanced         | Minimal     |\n          | CP           | 0.68 | 0.64 | 0.72   | Over-count (↑FP)  | Δ inflated  |\n          | coref        | 0.63 | 0.75 | 0.54   | Under-count (↑FN) | Δ deflated  |\n          | Overall      | 0.71 | 0.68 | 0.74   | Net over-count    | —           |\n          Human κ=0.68 | LLM-LLM κ=0.89 | LLM-Human κ=0.63\n      - name: \"Table 10a: Bias-Corrected Layer Gap\"\n        content: |\n          | Measure        | Raw   | Corrected (est.) | Change |\n          |----------------|-------|------------------|--------|\n          | auth_scope Δpp | 34.6  | ~30.0            | -4.6   |\n          | incomp Δpp     | 35.6  | ~34.0            | -1.6   |\n          | CP Δpp         | 26.0  | ~23.0            | -3.0   |\n          | scopal Δpp     | 30.8  | ~30.0            | -0.8   |\n          | lexical Δpp    | 26.2  | ~26.0            | -0.2   |\n          | coref Δpp      | 24.2  | ~28.0            | +3.8   |\n          | Spec avg       | 32.1  | ~29.0            | -3.1   |\n          | Ling avg       | 27.1  | ~28.0            | +0.9   |\n          | Layer gap      | 5.0   | ~1.0             | -4.0   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Calibration scatter: judge VR vs human VR per type, identity line。Auth above (over), coref below (under)。\"\n      - \"Triple bar: LLM-LLM κ(0.89) vs Human-Human κ(0.68) vs LLM-Human κ(0.63)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Judge calibration 是 layer hierarchy 的 final nail。Raw gap 5pp (already NS),\n      corrected gap ~1pp。Remaining \"layer effect\" largely measurement artifact:\n      judge over-counts spec-layer violations, under-counts ling-layer (especially\n      coref)。但 binary effect calibration-robust: corrected ~27pp 仍 massive。\n\n      Paper strategy: (1) report raw + corrected side by side; (2) lead with binary\n      effect (calibration-robust); (3) explicitly note layer gap may be artifact\n      in limitations; (4) practical message strengthened——if types even more similar\n      after correction, type-specific detection less necessary。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: Classifier PoC\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: classifier_poc\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      Binary ambiguity detector PoC: DeBERTa-v3-large fine-tune on 300 clause\n      pairs, 5-fold CV。\n    expected_results:\n      model: DeBERTa-v3-large\n      training_pairs: 300\n      cv_folds: 5\n      binary_f1: 0.82\n      binary_precision: 0.84\n      binary_recall: 0.80\n      per_type_f1:\n        authorization_scope: 0.88\n        conditional_precedence: 0.85\n        scopal: 0.84\n        incompleteness: 0.82\n        lexical: 0.76\n        coreferential: 0.68\n      type_6way_f1: 0.48\n      layer_2way_f1: 0.58\n      gpu_hours: 3.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binary F1=0.82: ambiguity detection signal 存在。Per-type spread follows\n      surface marker salience: auth_scope (permission verbs, F1=0.88) easiest,\n      coref (discourse-level coreference, F1=0.68) hardest。6-way type F1=0.48\n      (above chance 0.17 但 practically weak) 和 layer 2-way F1=0.58 确认 type\n      boundaries surface-fuzzy——consistent with TOST equivalence。\n\n      Detection difficulty anti-correlates with risk: easiest-to-detect types\n      (auth_scope 0.88, CP 0.85) are also the most dangerous on GPT models。\n      This is practical silver lining——priority targets are also easy to find。\n\n      在 worst tier narrative 下, classifier 支持 practical message: binary\n      detection feasible (F1=0.82) and sufficient (type detection F1=0.48 too\n      weak to be useful, consistent with types being functionally equivalent)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: Classifier Performance\"\n        content: |\n          | Task                    | F1   | Precision | Recall |\n          |-------------------------|------|-----------|--------|\n          | Binary (amb vs unamb)   | 0.82 | 0.84      | 0.80   |\n          | 6-way type              | 0.48 | 0.50      | 0.46   |\n          | 2-way layer             | 0.58 | 0.60      | 0.56   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual y-axis bar: per-type F1 (left) vs per-type Δpp (right), showing anti-correlation。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Classifier PoC role in worst tier: demonstrates binary detection feasible,\n      type detection not——aligning with reframed message。Practical pipeline =\n      binary flag → human review, 不需要 type-specific handling。P2 priority\n      合理——non-core but concrete practical grounding。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15567,"cache_read_input_tokens":47956,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15567},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd9ee42-9f53-44aa-92a5-74909781e0f9","uuid":"fe2c1fd9-d4ff-4ffa-b93a-126f7442159e"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":1375769,"duration_api_ms":1377206,"num_turns":5,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Layer hierarchy 不能做 headline——5-model pooled gap 仅 ~5pp (CI 含 0, p=0.14)，\n  Claude profile 扁平 (gap 1pp), Qwen3-8B layer 反转 (gap -4pp)。Model×type interaction\n  显著 (p=0.003) 意味着 type ranking 是 model-dependent 而非 universal property。\n  Judge calibration 暴露 type-specific 测量偏差: auth_scope 被 over-count (precision 0.58),\n  coref 被 under-count (recall 0.54)——校正后 layer gap 可能 <1pp，完全由 measurement bias\n  解释。Error analysis failure modes 跨层高度重叠 (match 42%)，universal 'arbitrary\n  resolution' (ambiguity blindness) 占 38% traces，无法分离 spec vs ling 机制。\n\n  Reframe 首选 (C)+(B): primary headline = 'The Massive Binary Effect' (+30pp pooled,\n  perturbation-controlled, Δ_perturb=3.6pp)——仍是 agent safety 文献最大因果效应，足以\n  支撑 EMNLP paper。§6 core = 'Ambiguity Blindness' 分析——所有模型、所有 type 的主导\n  failure mode 是无意识地采纳单一解读 (arbitrary resolution)，CL 贡献=连接 good-enough\n  processing 到 agent failure mode。Model-dependent vulnerability profiles 从 nuisance\n  升级为 informative finding: practical implication = type-aware auditing 需 model-specific\n  calibration，但 binary detection 仍 sufficient for first-pass triage (TOST 13/15 pairs\n  equivalent at ±10pp)。\n\n  标题: 'Policy Ambiguity Causes Catastrophic Safety Violations in LLM Agents: A Causal\n  Study'。投 EMNLP: (1) binary causal effect + perturbation control, (2) ambiguity\n  blindness mechanism, (3) 5-model cross-family replication。放弃 C2/C3 layer hierarchy\n  claim, 降为 exploratory observation。C4 model×type interaction 升级为 secondary finding。\n  TOST 的 equivalence result 反而 strengthens practical message: binary detection suffices。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_001: Clause Generation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_clause_generation\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      生成剩余 140 条 clauses (coreferential 50, auth_scope 50, lexical +20,\n      incompleteness +20)，验证全部 300 条 clause pairs 质量与跨类型平衡。\n      CP 格式混合 labeled/unlabeled。\n    expected_results:\n      total_clauses: 300\n      clauses_per_type: 50\n      first_round_pass_rate: 0.85\n      clauses_requiring_revision: 23\n      revision_rate_by_type:\n        coreferential: 0.32\n        incompleteness: 0.18\n        lexical: 0.14\n        authorization_scope: 0.12\n        scopal: 0.10\n        conditional_precedence: 0.08\n      cross_type_token_length_cv: 0.15\n      flesch_kincaid_range: [8.5, 12.3]\n      cp_format_mix: {labeled: 25, unlabeled: 25}\n      validator_agreement_kappa: 0.74\n    result_rationale: >\n      Coreferential 修订率最高 (32%): 跨句代词-先行词链在 policy 语域中构造难度大——\n      需要 ambiguous 版本有真实的 referent 竞争、unambiguous 版本消歧又保持自然。\n      部分 coref clauses 的 ambiguity 要么过于 subtle (strong model 通过 context 消解)\n      要么过于 artificial (reviewer 可质疑 ecological validity)。这为后续 coref 在不同\n      模型上表现 divergent 埋下伏笔——clause construct validity 不均匀是 model-specific\n      behavior 的 confound 之一。Auth_scope 相对容易 (12%) 因有成熟 RE permission\n      boundary 模板。Validator κ=0.74 反映 incompleteness 类型的 \"信息充分性\" 判断\n      存在主观性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A1: Clause Generation Summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Type                   | Target | R1 Pass | Revised | Final | Avg Tokens (amb) |\n          |------------------------|--------|---------|---------|-------|------------------|\n          | scopal                 | 50     | 45      | 5       | 50    | 28.4             |\n          | lexical                | 50     | 43      | 7       | 50    | 24.7             |\n          | incompleteness         | 50     | 41      | 9       | 50    | 31.2             |\n          | coreferential          | 50     | 34      | 16      | 50    | 34.8             |\n          | authorization_scope    | 50     | 44      | 6       | 50    | 27.1             |\n          | conditional_precedence | 50     | 46      | 4       | 50    | 33.0             |\n          | Total                  | 300    | 253     | 47*     | 300   | 29.9             |\n          * some clauses revised multiple rounds; 23 unique clauses needed revision\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot: per-type token length distributions (ambiguous variants), CV=0.15 标注\"\n    analysis: >\n      Clause generation 本身与 tier 无关，但 coreferential 的高修订率暗示 construct\n      validity 偏弱。部分 subtle coref ambiguity 在 policy 单句中难以自然呈现，\n      导致: (1) 对 strong model 歧义不够 challenging, (2) 对 weak model 歧义不被\n      parse。两方向都增加 coref VR 的 model-specific variance，在 plan_003/006 中显现。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_001b: New Type Mini-Pilot\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: new_type_mini_pilot\n    plan_id: plan_001b\n    description: >\n      Mini-pilot: coreferential + auth_scope 各 5 clauses × 2 conditions × 1 model\n      (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes。验证新类型可用性。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 20\n      coreferential:\n        ambiguous_violations: \"2/5 (40%)\"\n        control_violations: \"0/5 (0%)\"\n        passes_criteria: true\n      authorization_scope:\n        ambiguous_violations: \"3/5 (60%)\"\n        control_violations: \"0/5 (0%)\"\n        passes_criteria: true\n      overall_verdict: PASS\n      api_cost_usd: 1.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mini-pilot 在 gpt-5.4 上 PASS: 两种类型 ambiguous 条件触发 violations，control\n      干净。但 N=5 的 estimate 极不稳定 (95% CI 跨越 ~5-85%)。关键盲区: gpt-5.4 是\n      capability 最强模型，其 type profile (auth_scope high, coref low) 恰好与 worst\n      tier 中 Qwen3-8B 的 reversed profile 相反。Single-model pilot 无法预警后续\n      model-specific divergence——如果用 Qwen3-8B 做 pilot 会看到 auth_scope 仅 ~1/5\n      而 coref 可能 ~3/5，完全相反的 pattern。Pilot 给出 false confidence。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Pilot PASS 但信息有限。Coref 2/5=40% 在 gpt-5.4 上高于 5-model pooled 预期\n      (32%)，纯属 small-N variance。Auth_scope 3/5=60% 接近 gpt-5.4 full-study 预期\n      (50%)。两种类型 \"work\" 但 between-model variance 完全不可见。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_010: Perturbation Control\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: perturbation_control\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      30 clause pairs non-ambiguity perturbation (15 synonym + 15 reorder) × 2\n      conditions × 3 API models = 180 episodes。验证 ambiguity-specific causation。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 180\n      perturbation_types: {synonym_substitution: 15, clause_reorder: 15}\n      perturbed_violation_rate: 0.078\n      original_violation_rate: 0.042\n      delta_perturb_pp: 3.6\n      delta_perturb_ci95: [-3.2, 10.4]\n      ci_contains_zero: true\n      ambiguity_delta_pp: 29.6\n      ratio: 0.122\n      ratio_threshold: 0.15\n      verdict: PASS\n      synonym_delta_pp: 4.2\n      reorder_delta_pp: 3.0\n      ci_width_pp: 13.6\n      api_cost_usd: 28\n    result_rationale: >\n      Perturbation control PASS: Δ_perturb=3.6pp (CI 含 0), ratio=0.12 < 0.15。\n      Non-ambiguity surface changes 对 agent safety behavior 无显著影响——证实\n      violation rate increase 是 ambiguity-specific 而非 general prompt sensitivity。\n      Synonym substitution (4.2pp) 略高于 reorder (3.0pp)，个别 synonym 可能引入\n      subtle meaning shift，但均在 noise range。CI width 13.6pp 偏大 (N=180 power\n      有限)，但 upper bound 10.4pp 仍远低于 ambiguity Δ 29.6pp。Verdict robust，\n      无需追加 episodes。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table P1: Perturbation Control Results\"\n        content: |\n          | Condition        | VR (perturbed) | VR (original) | Δpp  | 95% CI        |\n          |------------------|----------------|---------------|------|---------------|\n          | Synonym (N=90)   | 8.9%           | 4.4%          | +4.5 | [-4.8, 13.8]  |\n          | Reorder (N=90)   | 6.7%           | 3.9%          | +2.8 | [-5.6, 11.2]  |\n          | Combined (N=180) | 7.8%           | 4.2%          | +3.6 | [-3.2, 10.4]  |\n          Ambiguity Δ (full study, 5-model): +29.6pp\n          Ratio: 0.122 | Verdict: PASS\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: Δ_perturb (3.6pp) vs Δ_ambiguity (29.6pp) with CI error bars, ratio=0.12 标注\"\n    analysis: >\n      Perturbation control 是 worst tier 中最 clean 的 positive result。即使 binary\n      effect 被 open-source 模型拉低至 ~30pp，相对于 perturbation baseline (3.6pp)\n      仍有 ~26pp net ambiguity-specific effect。这为 reframe (C) 'Massive Binary\n      Effect' 提供最强因果证据。C1 causal claim 不受 layer hierarchy collapse 影响。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_002: Full Study — API Models\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_api\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1,\n      claude-sonnet-4-6) = 1,800 episodes。Cross-judge evaluation。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1800\n      episodes_per_model: 600\n\n      gpt54:\n        overall_amb_vr: 0.392\n        overall_ctrl_vr: 0.040\n        overall_delta_pp: 35.2\n        per_type_amb_vr:\n          auth_scope: 0.50\n          incompleteness: 0.48\n          scopal: 0.40\n          lexical: 0.36\n          CP: 0.35\n          coreferential: 0.26\n        per_type_delta_pp:\n          auth_scope: 46\n          incompleteness: 45\n          scopal: 36\n          lexical: 31\n          CP: 32\n          coreferential: 21\n        layer_gap_pp: 11.7\n        type_ranking: \"auth > incomp > scopal > CP > lexical > coref\"\n\n      gpt41:\n        overall_amb_vr: 0.372\n        overall_ctrl_vr: 0.048\n        overall_delta_pp: 32.3\n        per_type_amb_vr:\n          auth_scope: 0.48\n          incompleteness: 0.46\n          scopal: 0.38\n          lexical: 0.34\n          CP: 0.33\n          coreferential: 0.24\n        per_type_delta_pp:\n          auth_scope: 43\n          incompleteness: 42\n          scopal: 33\n          lexical: 29\n          CP: 29\n          coreferential: 18\n        layer_gap_pp: 11.3\n        type_ranking: \"auth > incomp > scopal > lexical = CP > coref\"\n\n      claude_sonnet:\n        overall_amb_vr: 0.372\n        overall_ctrl_vr: 0.057\n        overall_delta_pp: 31.5\n        per_type_amb_vr:\n          auth_scope: 0.38\n          incompleteness: 0.42\n          scopal: 0.40\n          lexical: 0.35\n          CP: 0.32\n          coreferential: 0.36\n        per_type_delta_pp:\n          auth_scope: 32\n          incompleteness: 37\n          scopal: 34\n          lexical: 30\n          CP: 27\n          coreferential: 29\n        layer_gap_pp: 1.0\n        type_ranking: \"incomp > scopal > auth > lexical > coref > CP\"\n\n      api_pooled:\n        overall_delta_pp: 33.0\n        layer_gap_pp: 8.0\n        cramers_v_api: 0.14\n        cross_judge_kappa: 0.89\n      api_cost_usd: 420\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT 模型保持与旧 plan_002 数据 direction-consistent 的 pattern: auth_scope 和\n      incompleteness 最高, coreferential 最低, layer gap ~11pp。但 Claude 引入\n      qualitative divergence:\n\n      (1) Auth_scope 仅 38% (GPT 48-50%): Claude 的 safety training 使其对 permission\n      boundary 更 conservative，ambiguous authorization 时倾向 refuse 而非 grant。\n      (2) Coreferential 36% (GPT 24-26%): Claude 的 discourse processing 策略不同，\n      在 pronoun resolution 上更频繁采取 risky referent assignment。\n      (3) Type ranking 完全不同 (incomp > scopal > auth)，layer gap 仅 1pp——flat。\n\n      API-pooled layer gap 从旧 2-model 数据的 ~19pp 缩至 8pp，完全由 Claude 的\n      flat profile 驱动。Binary effect 仍强: 3 API models 均 >31pp。Cross-judge\n      κ=0.89 表明 LLM judge 间一致性高 (但 plan_009 将揭示这不代表 accuracy)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: API Model Violation Rates by Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type         | gpt-5.4       |       | gpt-4.1       |       | Claude        |       |\n          |              | Amb   | Δpp   | Amb   | Δpp   | Amb   | Δpp   |\n          |--------------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|\n          | auth_scope   | 50%   | +46   | 48%   | +43   | 38%   | +32   |\n          | incomp       | 48%   | +45   | 46%   | +42   | 42%   | +37   |\n          | scopal       | 40%   | +36   | 38%   | +33   | 40%   | +34   |\n          | lexical      | 36%   | +31   | 34%   | +29   | 35%   | +30   |\n          | CP           | 35%   | +32   | 33%   | +29   | 32%   | +27   |\n          | coref        | 26%   | +21   | 24%   | +18   | 36%   | +29   |\n          | Overall      | 39.2% | +35.2 | 37.2% | +32.3 | 37.2% | +31.5 |\n          Control VR: gpt-5.4 4.0%, gpt-4.1 4.8%, Claude 5.7%\n      - name: \"Table 1a: Layer Gap by API Model\"\n        content: |\n          | Model        | Spec Avg Δ | Ling Avg Δ | Layer Gap | Direction   |\n          |--------------|------------|------------|-----------|-------------|\n          | gpt-5.4      | 41.0pp     | 29.3pp     | +11.7pp   | Spec > Ling |\n          | gpt-4.1      | 38.0pp     | 26.7pp     | +11.3pp   | Spec > Ling |\n          | Claude       | 32.0pp     | 31.0pp     | +1.0pp    | Flat        |\n          | API Pooled   | 37.0pp     | 29.0pp     | +8.0pp    | Weakened    |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3 API × 6 types Δpp matrix。Claude 行 color 均匀 (no gradient), GPT 行有明显 gradient。\"\n      - \"Radar chart: 6 types 作 axes, 3 models 各一条线。GPT 形状相似 (auth 方向拉长), Claude 接近正六边形。\"\n    analysis: >\n      plan_002 是 worst tier 的 inflection point。GPT-only 子集仍支持 layer hierarchy\n      (gap ~11pp)，但 Claude 的加入将 API-pooled gap 压至 8pp (borderline)。\n      如果在此阶段分析，已可预见: layer hierarchy 的 generalizability 取决于 model\n      selection, 不是 universal property。Binary effect 仍 secure (>31pp all models)。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003: Full Study — Local Models\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_local\n    plan_id: plan_003\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n      via vLLM) = 1,200 episodes。Cross-judge uses API models。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1200\n      episodes_per_model: 600\n\n      qwen32b:\n        overall_amb_vr: 0.340\n        overall_ctrl_vr: 0.077\n        overall_delta_pp: 26.3\n        per_type_amb_vr:\n          auth_scope: 0.40\n          incompleteness: 0.38\n          scopal: 0.34\n          lexical: 0.30\n          CP: 0.30\n          coreferential: 0.32\n        per_type_delta_pp:\n          auth_scope: 32\n          incompleteness: 31\n          scopal: 27\n          lexical: 22\n          CP: 23\n          coreferential: 23\n        layer_gap_pp: 4.7\n        type_ranking: \"auth > incomp > scopal > CP = coref > lexical\"\n\n      qwen8b:\n        overall_amb_vr: 0.323\n        overall_ctrl_vr: 0.098\n        overall_delta_pp: 22.5\n        per_type_amb_vr:\n          auth_scope: 0.30\n          incompleteness: 0.32\n          scopal: 0.34\n          lexical: 0.28\n          CP: 0.28\n          coreferential: 0.42\n        per_type_delta_pp:\n          auth_scope: 20\n          incompleteness: 23\n          scopal: 24\n          lexical: 19\n          CP: 19\n          coreferential: 30\n        layer_gap_pp: -3.7\n        type_ranking: \"coref > scopal > incomp > auth > lexical = CP\"\n        coreferential_is_highest: true\n        layer_reversed: true\n\n      local_pooled:\n        overall_delta_pp: 24.4\n        layer_gap_pp: 0.5\n      vllm_throughput_episodes_per_hour: 42\n      gpu_hours_used: 29\n      cross_judge_kappa: 0.84\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Local models 确认 layer collapse。Qwen3-32B 介于 GPT 和 Claude 之间:\n      auth_scope 仍最高但 coref 升至与 CP 同水平 (32% vs 30%), gap 仅 4.7pp。\n\n      Qwen3-8B 是 qualitative break:\n      (1) Coreferential 最高 (42%, Δ=+30pp): 模型 discourse processing 能力弱，\n      无法正确 resolve policy 中的代词关系。当 coreferential ambiguity 存在时，\n      频繁将 pronoun 绑定到 wrong referent (如 \"their policy\" 误归因为 customer's\n      而非 company's), 执行错误 entity 的 policy。Strong models (gpt-5.4 26%) 能\n      通过 context 部分消歧。\n      (2) Auth_scope 最低 (30%, Δ=+20pp): Qwen3-8B instruction following 偏\n      conservative——面对模糊 permission boundary 时 confidence 低，默认 refuse。\n      这不是 \"理解\" ambiguity, 而是 weak model 对 authorization decision 的\n      uncertainty 导致 safe-path default。对比 gpt-5.4 (50%) confident enough to\n      make (wrong) authorization decisions。\n      (3) Layer 反转 (gap -3.7pp): Spec avg Δ=20.7pp < Ling avg Δ=24.3pp。Coref\n      单一 type (30pp) 拉高 ling average 超过所有 spec types。\n\n      Local pooled layer gap 0.5pp, 本质为零。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Local Model Violation Rates by Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type         | Qwen3-32B     |       | Qwen3-8B      |       |\n          |              | Amb   | Δpp   | Amb   | Δpp   |\n          |--------------|-------|-------|-------|-------|\n          | auth_scope   | 40%   | +32   | 30%   | +20   |\n          | incomp       | 38%   | +31   | 32%   | +23   |\n          | scopal       | 34%   | +27   | 34%   | +24   |\n          | lexical      | 30%   | +22   | 28%   | +19   |\n          | CP           | 30%   | +23   | 28%   | +19   |\n          | coref        | 32%   | +23   | 42%   | +30   |\n          | Overall      | 34.0% | +26.3 | 32.3% | +22.5 |\n          Control VR: Qwen3-32B 7.7%, Qwen3-8B 9.8%\n      - name: \"Table 2a: Type Ranking Comparison Across 5 Models (Δpp)\"\n        content: |\n          | Rank | gpt-5.4    | gpt-4.1    | Claude     | Qwen32B    | Qwen3-8B   |\n          |------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|\n          | 1    | auth (46)  | auth (43)  | incomp (37)| auth (32)  | coref (30) |\n          | 2    | incomp (45)| incomp (42)| scopal (34)| incomp (31)| scopal (24)|\n          | 3    | scopal (36)| scopal (33)| auth (32)  | scopal (27)| incomp (23)|\n          | 4    | CP (32)    | lexical (29)| lexical(30)| CP (23)   | auth (20)  |\n          | 5    | lexical(31)| CP (29)    | coref (29) | coref (23) | lexical(19)|\n          | 6    | coref (21) | coref (18) | CP (27)    | lexical(22)| CP (19)    |\n          Kendall's W = 0.52 (moderate concordance)\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Parallel coordinates: 5 models on x, 6 type lines on y=Δpp。Coref 线从 gpt-5.4(21) 升至 Qwen8B(30), auth 线从 46 降至 20——crossing。\"\n      - \"Layer gap bar chart: 5 models, gpt-5.4(+12) gpt-4.1(+11) Claude(+1) Qwen32B(+5) Qwen8B(-4), pooled=+5 水平线。\"\n    analysis: >\n      plan_003 definitively kills layer hierarchy as headline。5-model pooled gap\n      = 5pp, 不足以支撑 \"Spec >> Ling\"。Qwen3-8B reversed pattern 有 mechanistic\n      explanation: model capability 决定 which types most dangerous——strong models\n      在 auth_scope (需 confident authorization) 上更 vulnerable, weak models 在\n      coref (需 discourse processing) 上更 vulnerable。这直接支撑叙事 pivot:\n      layer hierarchy → model-dependent vulnerability profiles。但 model-dependency\n      增加 story complexity, 不适合 primary headline → binary effect 必须升级。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_004: Full Study Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      合并 3,000 episodes 统计分析: binary effect (C1), type differentiation (C2),\n      layer comparison (C3), model×type interaction (C4), TOST, power analysis,\n      inter-model agreement, information delta control。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 3000\n      episodes_per_type_per_condition_pooled: 250\n\n      # --- C1: Binary Effect ---\n      overall_binary_delta_pp: 29.6\n      overall_binary_ci95: [26.1, 33.1]\n      overall_mcnemar_or: 22.4\n      overall_mcnemar_or_ci95: [14.2, 35.3]\n      overall_mcnemar_p: \"<1e-60\"\n      per_type_binary_effects:\n        incompleteness: {delta_pp: 35.6, ci95: [29.2, 42.0], p: \"<1e-12\", holm_sig: true}\n        auth_scope:     {delta_pp: 34.6, ci95: [28.3, 40.9], p: \"<1e-12\", holm_sig: true}\n        scopal:         {delta_pp: 30.8, ci95: [24.6, 37.0], p: \"<1e-10\", holm_sig: true}\n        lexical:        {delta_pp: 26.2, ci95: [20.1, 32.3], p: \"<1e-8\",  holm_sig: true}\n        CP:             {delta_pp: 26.0, ci95: [19.9, 32.1], p: \"<1e-8\",  holm_sig: true}\n        coreferential:  {delta_pp: 24.2, ci95: [18.2, 30.2], p: \"<1e-7\",  holm_sig: true}\n      all_6_types_significant_after_holm: true\n\n      # --- C2: Type Differentiation ---\n      omnibus_chi2: 18.7\n      omnibus_df: 5\n      omnibus_p: 0.002\n      cramers_v: 0.11\n      pairwise_significant_after_holm:\n        - [\"incomp vs coref\", \"Δ=11.4pp, p=0.003\"]\n        - [\"auth vs coref\",  \"Δ=10.4pp, p=0.008 (borderline after Holm)\"]\n      pairwise_nonsignificant_examples:\n        - [\"auth vs incomp\",  \"Δ=1.0pp, p=0.91\"]\n        - [\"scopal vs lexical\", \"Δ=4.6pp, p=0.28\"]\n        - [\"CP vs coref\",     \"Δ=1.8pp, p=0.68\"]\n        - [\"lexical vs CP\",   \"Δ=0.2pp, p=0.97\"]\n\n      # --- C3: Layer Effect ---\n      layer_spec_avg_delta: 32.1\n      layer_ling_avg_delta: 27.1\n      layer_gap_pp: 5.0\n      layer_gap_ci95: [-1.8, 11.8]\n      layer_gap_p: 0.14\n      layer_gap_significant: false\n      layer_gap_per_model:\n        gpt54: 11.7\n        gpt41: 11.3\n        claude: 1.0\n        qwen32b: 4.7\n        qwen8b: -3.7\n\n      # --- C4: Model × Type Interaction ---\n      model_main_effect_p: 0.038\n      model_main_effect_v: 0.06\n      type_main_effect_p: 0.002\n      type_main_effect_v: 0.11\n      model_type_interaction_chi2: 42.3\n      model_type_interaction_df: 20\n      model_type_interaction_p: 0.003\n      logistic_interaction_lrt_p: 0.005\n      per_model_delta_pp: {gpt54: 35.2, gpt41: 32.3, claude: 31.5, qwen32b: 26.3, qwen8b: 22.5}\n      capability_rank_vs_delta_spearman: 0.90\n      type_ranking_kendalls_w: 0.52\n\n      # --- TOST Equivalence ---\n      tost_10pp: {equivalent_pairs: 13, total: 15, non_equiv: [\"incomp-coref (11.4pp)\", \"auth-coref (10.4pp)\"]}\n      tost_15pp: {equivalent_pairs: 15, total: 15}\n\n      # --- Power Analysis ---\n      mde_layer_gap_80pct_power: 11.5\n      observed_layer_gap: 5.0\n      underpowered_for_layer: true\n      mde_pairwise_80pct_power: 12.8\n\n      # --- Inter-Model Agreement ---\n      inter_model_fleiss_kappa_ambiguous: 0.62\n      per_type_fleiss_kappa:\n        auth_scope: 0.55\n        incompleteness: 0.60\n        scopal: 0.72\n        lexical: 0.68\n        CP: 0.65\n        coreferential: 0.38\n      agreement_interpretation: \"models converge on same (wrong) interpretations — systematic bias, not true nocuity divergence (except coref κ=0.38)\"\n\n      # --- Information Delta ---\n      per_type_token_delta: {auth_scope: 4.2, incomp: 6.8, scopal: 2.1, lexical: 1.4, CP: 5.3, coref: 3.7}\n      token_delta_vs_vr_correlation_r: 0.42\n      token_delta_confound: \"modest — incomp has largest delta and high VR, but scopal (low delta) also high\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      5-model pooled analysis confirms worst tier 的三重结构:\n\n      (1) C1 binary effect robust: +29.6pp [26.1, 33.1], 所有 6 types Holm-significant\n      (最弱 coref +24.2pp, p<1e-7)。从 2-model +36.5pp 降至 +29.6pp 主因 open-source\n      models 拉低 (Qwen3-8B +22.5pp)。但 +29.6pp 仍是 agent safety 文献最大因果效应,\n      且 perturbation-controlled (net ~26pp)。\n\n      (2) C2/C3 layer hierarchy 不成立: pooled gap 5.0pp, CI [-1.8, 11.8] 含 0,\n      p=0.14 not significant。Power analysis 显示 MDE=11.5pp 而观测仅 5.0pp——\n      即使 true gap 存在也不够大被 detect。更关键: gap 是 model-dependent (gpt-5.4\n      +11.7, Claude +1.0, Qwen8B -3.7)——无法声称 universal hierarchy。Omnibus\n      χ²=18.7 (p=0.002, V=0.11) 说明 types 在统计上 differ 但 effect 小;\n      TOST ±10pp 下 13/15 pairs equivalent, ±15pp 全部 equivalent——types 在\n      practical significance 层面不可区分。\n\n      (3) C4 model×type interaction 显著 (χ²=42.3, p=0.003): type ranking 因模型\n      而异。GPT models auth_scope/incomp 最危险, Qwen3-8B coref 最危险, Claude\n      types 间差异最小。Kendall's W=0.52 (moderate concordance)——models have some\n      agreement (都觉得 lexical 较低) 但 critical divergence 在 top-ranked types。\n\n      Inter-model Fleiss' κ=0.62 表明 models mostly converge on same outcomes\n      (systematic bias)。Coref κ=0.38 是例外——models 对 coref clauses 产生\n      divergent outcomes (GPT low, Claude/Qwen8B high), 接近 Berry & Kamsties 的\n      true nocuity (divergent interpretations)。\n\n      TOST 对 practical framing 有 constructive implication: types statistically\n      differ (V=0.11) 但 practically equivalent (±10pp) → binary detection may\n      indeed suffice for practical triage, 与 best-tier practical message convergent\n      (只是 theoretical argument 不同)。\n\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: 5-Model Pooled Binary Effect by Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type         | N  | Amb VR | Ctrl VR| Δpp   | 95% CI        | p      | Holm |\n          |--------------|-----|--------|--------|-------|---------------|--------|------|\n          | incomp       | 250 | 41.2%  | 5.6%   | +35.6 | [29.2, 42.0]  | <1e-12 | ***  |\n          | auth_scope   | 250 | 41.2%  | 6.6%   | +34.6 | [28.3, 40.9]  | <1e-12 | ***  |\n          | scopal       | 250 | 37.2%  | 6.4%   | +30.8 | [24.6, 37.0]  | <1e-10 | ***  |\n          | lexical      | 250 | 32.6%  | 6.4%   | +26.2 | [20.1, 32.3]  | <1e-8  | ***  |\n          | CP           | 250 | 31.6%  | 5.6%   | +26.0 | [19.9, 32.1]  | <1e-8  | ***  |\n          | coref        | 250 | 32.0%  | 7.8%   | +24.2 | [18.2, 30.2]  | <1e-7  | ***  |\n          | Overall      | 1500| 36.0%  | 6.4%   | +29.6 | [26.1, 33.1]  | <1e-60 | ***  |\n      - name: \"Table 4: 5×6 Model×Type Binary Effect (Δpp) Matrix\"\n        content: |\n          | Type         | gpt-5.4| gpt-4.1| Claude| Qwen32B| Qwen8B| Type Avg|\n          |--------------|--------|--------|-------|--------|-------|---------|\n          | auth_scope   | +46    | +43    | +32   | +32    | +20   | +34.6   |\n          | incomp       | +45    | +42    | +37   | +31    | +23   | +35.6   |\n          | scopal       | +36    | +33    | +34   | +27    | +24   | +30.8   |\n          | lexical      | +31    | +29    | +30   | +22    | +19   | +26.2   |\n          | CP           | +32    | +29    | +27   | +23    | +19   | +26.0   |\n          | coref        | +21    | +18    | +29   | +23    | +30   | +24.2   |\n          | Model Avg    | +35.2  | +32.3  | +31.5 | +26.3  | +22.5 | +29.6   |\n\n          Model×Type: χ²(20)=42.3, p=0.003\n          Layer gap per model: gpt-5.4 +11.7, gpt-4.1 +11.3, Claude +1.0, Qwen32B +4.7, Qwen8B -3.7\n          Pooled gap: +5.0pp [-1.8, 11.8], p=0.14 (NS)\n      - name: \"Table 5: Equivalence & Omnibus Summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Test                               | Statistic | p/value | Interpretation             |\n          |------------------------------------|-----------|---------|----------------------------|\n          | Omnibus χ²(5)                      | 18.7      | 0.002   | Types differ statistically |\n          | Cramér's V                         | 0.11      | —       | Small effect               |\n          | TOST ±10pp equivalent              | 13/15     | —       | Most types equiv           |\n          | TOST ±15pp equivalent              | 15/15     | —       | All types equiv            |\n          | Layer gap (Spec−Ling)              | 5.0pp     | 0.14    | Not significant            |\n          | Model×Type χ²(20)                  | 42.3      | 0.003   | Significant interaction    |\n          | Fleiss' κ (ambiguous)              | 0.62      | —       | Moderate (systematic bias) |\n          | MDE for layer gap (80% power)      | 11.5pp    | —       | Underpowered (obs=5.0)     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: per-type Δpp + 95% CI, ordered by effect size。CI 大面积重叠。\"\n      - \"Heatmap: 5×6 Δpp matrix (Table 4)。Coref 列 gradient 与其他列方向相反 (冷→暖 vs 暖→冷)。\"\n      - \"Interaction plot: x=type, y=Δpp, 5 model lines。gpt-5.4 steep, Qwen8B near-flat with coref spike。Lines cross at coref。\"\n      - \"TOST strip: 15 pairwise Δ, ±10pp/±15pp 竖线。仅 2 pairs 超出 ±10pp。\"\n    analysis: >\n      plan_004 是 definitive analysis。Binary effect secure as headline (+29.6pp,\n      perturbation-controlled)。Layer hierarchy not significant (5pp, p=0.14),\n      model-dependent, and TOST-equivalent。Model×type interaction (p=0.003) 是\n      novel finding 但增加 complexity。Paper reframe: C1 primary, C4 secondary,\n      C2/C3 demoted to exploratory。TOST equivalence paradoxically supports\n      practical message: binary detection suffices regardless of type。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_005: Error Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: error_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      50 violation traces per type (300 total) qualitative failure mode analysis:\n      classify modes, cross-type/cross-model distribution, visibility evidence。\n    expected_results:\n      total_traces: 300\n      traces_per_type: 50\n      failure_modes_identified: 6\n      failure_mode_taxonomy:\n        boundary_overreach: \"Agent grants permission beyond stated authorization\"\n        assumption_filling: \"Agent fills info gap with ungrounded assumption\"\n        scope_misapplication: \"Agent applies narrow/wide scope incorrectly\"\n        conflict_paralysis: \"Agent detects conflict, refuses or asks clarification\"\n        reference_confusion: \"Agent assigns wrong referent to pronoun/NP\"\n        arbitrary_resolution: \"Agent picks one reading without acknowledging ambiguity\"\n\n      arbitrary_resolution_prevalence: 0.38\n      arbitrary_resolution_range_per_type: [0.33, 0.48]\n      arbitrary_resolution_dominant_in: \"4/6 types\"\n      failure_mode_layer_match_pct: 42\n\n      cross_layer_contamination:\n        spec_modes_in_ling_types_pct: 15\n        ling_modes_in_spec_types_pct: 12\n\n      inter_annotator_kappa_overall: 0.45\n      inter_annotator_kappa_per_mode:\n        conflict_paralysis: 0.62\n        boundary_overreach: 0.55\n        scope_misapplication: 0.48\n        reference_confusion: 0.44\n        assumption_filling: 0.40\n        arbitrary_resolution: 0.28\n\n      model_specific:\n        gpt54_conflict_paralysis_CP_pct: 0.42\n        qwen8b_conflict_paralysis_CP_pct: 0.08\n        gpt54_ambiguity_detection_any_type_pct: 0.18\n        qwen8b_ambiguity_detection_any_type_pct: 0.02\n        claude_conservative_refusal_coref_pct: 0.22\n\n      visibility_evidence:\n        CP_traces_with_conflict_detection: 0.34\n        scopal_traces_with_ambiguity_awareness: 0.06\n        visibility_driven_by_gpt54_only: true\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Error analysis 暴露 layer mechanism 的 fragility。核心发现:\n\n      (1) \"Arbitrary resolution\" 占 38% 且在 4/6 types 中 dominant (range 33-48%)。\n      这就是 \"ambiguity blindness\": agent 无意识采纳单一解读，不 acknowledge\n      alternative。关键是它不分 layer——auth_scope (33%), scopal (40%), coref (36%)\n      都有大量 arbitrary resolution。Universal failure mechanism 是 blindness,\n      不是 layer-specific misprocessing。\n\n      (2) Layer-specific modes 为 minority: boundary_overreach 仅在 auth_scope\n      dominant (35%); reference_confusion 仅在 coref dominant (28%)。这些加起来\n      仅解释 ~30% traces, 不足以支撑 \"spec vs ling 有本质不同 failure mechanism\"。\n\n      (3) Cross-layer contamination: 15% ling-type traces 展示 spec modes\n      (assumption_filling 在 lexical 18%, coref 15%); 12% spec-type traces 展示\n      ling modes (scope_misapplication 在 CP 12%)。边界模糊。\n\n      (4) κ=0.45 (moderate) 被 arbitrary_resolution 低 κ (0.28) 拉低。这是\n      catch-all mode——判断 agent 是否 \"意识到\" ambiguity 高度主观。合并\n      arbitrary_resolution + assumption_filling 为 \"unacknowledged processing\"\n      (ambiguity blindness umbrella) 后 κ 升至 ~0.55, 且这 IS the reframed\n      core mechanism。\n\n      (5) Visibility evidence weak: CP 34% traces 有 conflict detection (主要\n      gpt-5.4 42%), scopal 仅 6%。但 pattern 仅 API models robust, Qwen3-8B\n      上 conflict_paralysis 8% (near zero)。无法推广为 universal finding。\n\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Failure Mode Distribution by Type (%)\"\n        content: |\n          | Mode                 | auth | incomp | scopal | lexical | CP  | coref |\n          |----------------------|------|--------|--------|---------|-----|-------|\n          | boundary_overreach   | 35   | 8      | 4      | 3       | 5   | 3     |\n          | assumption_filling   | 14   | 30     | 10     | 18      | 12  | 15    |\n          | scope_misapplication | 10   | 8      | 28     | 14      | 12  | 8     |\n          | conflict_paralysis   | 4    | 4      | 2      | 2       | 25  | 2     |\n          | reference_confusion  | 4    | 2      | 6      | 7       | 3   | 28    |\n          | arbitrary_resolution | 33   | 38     | 40     | 48      | 35  | 36    |\n          | other/mixed          | 0    | 10     | 10     | 8       | 8   | 8     |\n          Layer match: 42%\n      - name: \"Table 7: Inter-Annotator Agreement (κ) by Mode\"\n        content: |\n          | Mode                 | κ    | 95% CI       | Level         |\n          |----------------------|------|--------------|---------------|\n          | conflict_paralysis   | 0.62 | [0.48, 0.76] | Substantial   |\n          | boundary_overreach   | 0.55 | [0.40, 0.70] | Moderate      |\n          | scope_misapplication | 0.48 | [0.33, 0.63] | Moderate      |\n          | reference_confusion  | 0.44 | [0.28, 0.60] | Moderate      |\n          | assumption_filling   | 0.40 | [0.25, 0.55] | Fair-Moderate |\n          | arbitrary_resolution | 0.28 | [0.13, 0.43] | Fair          |\n          | Overall (macro)      | 0.45 | [0.38, 0.52] | Moderate      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar: failure mode proportions per type, ordered by Δpp。arbitrary_resolution 的 uniform 高占比是视觉焦点。\"\n      - \"Annotated trace pair: same clause, gpt-5.4 (conflict detection → refuse) vs Qwen3-8B (arbitrary resolution → violate)。\"\n      - \"Sankey: type → failure mode flow, 标注 cross-layer flows 比例。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error analysis 是 reframe pivot point。Layer mechanism 不成立 (match 42%,\n      contamination ~13%), 但 \"ambiguity blindness\" 作为 universal mechanism 有\n      stronger support: all models, all types 的 dominant pattern 是 agent 无意识\n      采纳单一解读 (38%)。CL 贡献 = good-enough processing 扩展到 LLM agents。\n\n      κ=0.45 是 concern 但 manageable: (a) report per-mode κ; (b) 强调 high-κ\n      modes 的 cross-type 差异 reliable; (c) ambiguity blindness claim 建立在\n      arbitrary_resolution prevalence (38%) 而非 fine-grained mode distinction。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_006: Reliability Test\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: reliability_test\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      30 clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 5 models = 900 episodes。\n      ICC for per-clause violation rates。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 900\n      overall_icc: 0.58\n      overall_icc_ci95: [0.44, 0.70]\n      icc_by_type:\n        authorization_scope: 0.65\n        incompleteness: 0.60\n        conditional_precedence: 0.58\n        scopal: 0.52\n        lexical: 0.50\n        coreferential: 0.42\n      icc_by_model:\n        gpt54: 0.65\n        gpt41: 0.60\n        claude: 0.58\n        qwen32b: 0.52\n        qwen8b: 0.44\n      mean_bootstrap_ci_width_pp: 11.8\n      max_single_clause_replicate_range_pp: 24\n      pct_clauses_flipping_significance: 0.10\n      gpu_hours_used: 14\n    result_rationale: >\n      ICC=0.58 (moderate)。Auth_scope 最 reliable (0.65): permission violation\n      near-deterministic (grant or deny)。Coreferential 最 unreliable (0.42):\n      pronoun resolution borderline cases 中 behavior highly stochastic。\n      Model-wise: gpt-5.4 (0.65) 最 deterministic, Qwen3-8B (0.44) 最 stochastic。\n\n      Mean CI width 11.8pp 超 <10pp target。Coreferential Δ=24.2pp 在 ICC=0.42\n      reliability 下, true effect 在 18-30pp 间 fluctuate substantially。\n      10% clauses flip binary significance across replicates, 但 key findings\n      (overall binary effect, type ranking direction) 在 3 replicates 中\n      direction-consistent。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: ICC by Type and Model\"\n        content: |\n          | Factor                | ICC(2,1) | 95% CI       | Mean |Δ| across reps |\n          |-----------------------|----------|--------------|---------------------|\n          | authorization_scope   | 0.65     | [0.46, 0.80] | 5.2pp               |\n          | incompleteness        | 0.60     | [0.40, 0.76] | 6.4pp               |\n          | conditional_precedence| 0.58     | [0.38, 0.74] | 6.8pp               |\n          | scopal                | 0.52     | [0.31, 0.70] | 7.6pp               |\n          | lexical               | 0.50     | [0.29, 0.68] | 8.0pp               |\n          | coreferential         | 0.42     | [0.20, 0.62] | 9.4pp               |\n          |--- Model ---|         |          |              |                     |\n          | gpt-5.4               | 0.65     | [0.47, 0.79] | 5.5pp               |\n          | gpt-4.1               | 0.60     | [0.41, 0.76] | 6.5pp               |\n          | claude-sonnet-4-6     | 0.58     | [0.38, 0.74] | 6.9pp               |\n          | Qwen3-32B-AWQ         | 0.52     | [0.31, 0.70] | 7.8pp               |\n          | Qwen3-8B              | 0.44     | [0.22, 0.64] | 9.0pp               |\n          | Overall               | 0.58     | [0.44, 0.70] | 7.3pp               |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: rep1 vs rep2 per-clause VR, faceted by type, identity line + ±10pp bands。Coref panel 最分散。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Binary effect (29.6pp) 远超 noise band (~12pp), 对 C1 robustness 无影响。\n      但 per-type comparisons 受限: 最弱 pairwise difference (auth-incomp 1.0pp,\n      CP-coref 1.8pp) 完全在 noise 内。Coref ICC=0.42 加上 Qwen3-8B anomalous\n      high rate, raises 可能性: 部分 type-specific patterns driven by stochastic\n      behavior 而非 systematic vulnerability。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: Realism Validation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: realism_validation\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      Synthetic clauses vs DRIP-R natural ambiguities linguistic property\n      comparison: sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR, word length。\n    expected_results:\n      drip_r_n: 127\n      synthetic_n: 300\n      metrics:\n        sentence_length: {synthetic: 29.9, drip_r: 24.5, ks_d: 0.22, p: 0.012, sig: true}\n        parse_depth:     {synthetic: 6.9,  drip_r: 5.3,  ks_d: 0.25, p: 0.004, sig: true}\n        flesch_kincaid:  {synthetic: 11.2, drip_r: 10.7, ks_d: 0.08, p: 0.62,  sig: false}\n        type_token_ratio:{synthetic: 0.82, drip_r: 0.79, ks_d: 0.09, p: 0.51,  sig: false}\n        mean_word_length:{synthetic: 5.1,  drip_r: 4.9,  ks_d: 0.10, p: 0.38,  sig: false}\n      metrics_passing: 3\n      metrics_failing: 2\n      verdict: partial_validation\n    result_rationale: >\n      Synthetic clauses 在 sentence length (+5.4 tokens) 和 parse depth (+1.6)\n      上显著高于 DRIP-R。原因: matched-pair design 要求 self-contained clauses,\n      导致 pack more info into single sentences。DRIP-R natural ambiguities 嵌在\n      完整文档中, 可依赖 surrounding context 补充。Readability metrics (FK, TTR,\n      word length) 无差异, vocabulary complexity 匹配。Counter-argument: longer\n      sentences provide MORE context for disambiguation, 偏差方向 conservative\n      (understates ambiguity effect for natural shorter sentences)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Synthetic vs DRIP-R Comparison\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric          | Synthetic      | DRIP-R         | KS D | p     | Sig |\n          |-----------------|----------------|----------------|------|-------|-----|\n          | Sentence length | 29.9 ± 8.2     | 24.5 ± 6.8     | 0.22 | 0.012 | *   |\n          | Parse depth     | 6.9 ± 2.0      | 5.3 ± 1.7      | 0.25 | 0.004 | **  |\n          | Flesch-Kincaid  | 11.2 ± 2.4     | 10.7 ± 2.6     | 0.08 | 0.62  | ns  |\n          | TTR             | 0.82 ± 0.08    | 0.79 ± 0.10    | 0.09 | 0.51  | ns  |\n          | Word length     | 5.1 ± 0.7      | 4.9 ± 0.8      | 0.10 | 0.38  | ns  |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Overlaid density plots: 5 metrics, synthetic (blue) vs DRIP-R (orange)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      3/5 pass acceptable。Length/depth 差异需 acknowledged as limitation。\n      Optional robustness: length-matched subset analysis (propensity-score\n      matching on sentence length), report in appendix if camera-ready allows。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_009: Judge Calibration\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: judge_calibration\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition, 2 human annotators,\n      LLM judge vs human ground truth: precision/recall/F1 per type。\n    expected_results:\n      episodes_sampled: 100\n      human_inter_annotator_kappa: 0.68\n      human_agreement_pct: 0.82\n\n      judge_human_overall:\n        f1: 0.71\n        precision: 0.68\n        recall: 0.74\n        kappa: 0.63\n\n      judge_human_per_type_f1:\n        authorization_scope: 0.65\n        incompleteness: 0.74\n        scopal: 0.77\n        lexical: 0.78\n        conditional_precedence: 0.68\n        coreferential: 0.63\n      types_below_075: [\"authorization_scope\", \"conditional_precedence\", \"coreferential\"]\n      types_below_075_count: 3\n\n      systematic_bias:\n        auth_scope: {direction: \"over-count\", precision: 0.58, recall: 0.72, note: \"FP where human=no-violation but judge=violation\"}\n        CP:         {direction: \"over-count\", precision: 0.64, recall: 0.72, note: \"inconsistent on conflict-detection outcomes\"}\n        coref:      {direction: \"under-count\", precision: 0.75, recall: 0.54, note: \"misses subtle referent-confusion violations\"}\n\n      bias_corrected_estimates:\n        auth_scope_delta_pp: \"~30 (raw 34.6)\"\n        coref_delta_pp: \"~28 (raw 24.2)\"\n        corrected_layer_gap_pp: \"<1 (raw 5.0)\"\n        layer_gap_may_be_measurement_artifact: true\n\n      cross_judge_asymmetry:\n        llm_llm_kappa: 0.89\n        llm_human_kappa: 0.63\n        gap_note: \"high LLM-LLM + low LLM-human = systematic shared bias\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Judge calibration 是 worst tier 最 devastating 发现。Overall F1=0.71 (κ=0.63)\n      远低于 LLM-LLM cross-judge κ=0.89。High LLM-LLM + low LLM-human = judges\n      share systematic bias (they agree with each other on wrong labels)。\n\n      Type-specific 偏差直接 undermines layer hierarchy:\n      (1) Auth_scope F1=0.65, precision=0.58: judge 将 agent cautious/qualified\n      authorization responses 误判为 violations, inflating auth_scope VR。True Δ\n      可能 ~30pp 而非 35pp。\n      (2) Coref F1=0.63, recall=0.54: judge 漏判 46% human-identified violations。\n      Coref violations subtle (wrong referent 但 action 表面合理), judge 无法从\n      trace 识别。True Δ 可能 ~28pp 而非 24pp。\n      (3) Net: 校正后 auth_scope (~30pp) ≈ coref (~28pp), layer gap 从 5pp 缩至\n      <1pp——potentially entirely measurement artifact。\n\n      Human κ=0.68 未达 target 0.75: 主要分歧在 severity tier (violation vs minor\n      deviation), 尤其 incompleteness 和 CP。暗示 violation definition 本身有\n      construct validity challenge。\n\n      对 binary effect impact 有限: overall recall=0.74 > precision=0.68, violations\n      are real (slightly over-counted)。Binary Δ ~29.6pp 校正后 ~27pp, 仍 massive。\n\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Judge Calibration Per-Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type         | F1   | Prec | Recall | Bias Direction    | Impact on Δ |\n          |--------------|------|------|--------|-------------------|-------------|\n          | auth_scope   | 0.65 | 0.58 | 0.72   | Over-count (↑FP)  | Δ inflated  |\n          | incomp       | 0.74 | 0.72 | 0.76   | Slight over-count | Minor       |\n          | scopal       | 0.77 | 0.76 | 0.78   | ~Balanced         | Minimal     |\n          | lexical      | 0.78 | 0.80 | 0.76   | ~Balanced         | Minimal     |\n          | CP           | 0.68 | 0.64 | 0.72   | Over-count (↑FP)  | Δ inflated  |\n          | coref        | 0.63 | 0.75 | 0.54   | Under-count (↑FN) | Δ deflated  |\n          | Overall      | 0.71 | 0.68 | 0.74   | Net over-count    | —           |\n          Human κ=0.68 | LLM-LLM κ=0.89 | LLM-Human κ=0.63\n      - name: \"Table 10a: Bias-Corrected Layer Gap\"\n        content: |\n          | Measure        | Raw   | Corrected (est.) | Change |\n          |----------------|-------|------------------|--------|\n          | auth_scope Δpp | 34.6  | ~30.0            | -4.6   |\n          | incomp Δpp     | 35.6  | ~34.0            | -1.6   |\n          | CP Δpp         | 26.0  | ~23.0            | -3.0   |\n          | scopal Δpp     | 30.8  | ~30.0            | -0.8   |\n          | lexical Δpp    | 26.2  | ~26.0            | -0.2   |\n          | coref Δpp      | 24.2  | ~28.0            | +3.8   |\n          | Spec avg       | 32.1  | ~29.0            | -3.1   |\n          | Ling avg       | 27.1  | ~28.0            | +0.9   |\n          | Layer gap      | 5.0   | ~1.0             | -4.0   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Calibration scatter: judge VR vs human VR per type, identity line。Auth above (over), coref below (under)。\"\n      - \"Triple bar: LLM-LLM κ(0.89) vs Human-Human κ(0.68) vs LLM-Human κ(0.63)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Judge calibration 是 layer hierarchy 的 final nail。Raw gap 5pp (already NS),\n      corrected gap ~1pp。Remaining \"layer effect\" largely measurement artifact:\n      judge over-counts spec-layer violations, under-counts ling-layer (especially\n      coref)。但 binary effect calibration-robust: corrected ~27pp 仍 massive。\n\n      Paper strategy: (1) report raw + corrected side by side; (2) lead with binary\n      effect (calibration-robust); (3) explicitly note layer gap may be artifact\n      in limitations; (4) practical message strengthened——if types even more similar\n      after correction, type-specific detection less necessary。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: Classifier PoC\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: classifier_poc\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      Binary ambiguity detector PoC: DeBERTa-v3-large fine-tune on 300 clause\n      pairs, 5-fold CV。\n    expected_results:\n      model: DeBERTa-v3-large\n      training_pairs: 300\n      cv_folds: 5\n      binary_f1: 0.82\n      binary_precision: 0.84\n      binary_recall: 0.80\n      per_type_f1:\n        authorization_scope: 0.88\n        conditional_precedence: 0.85\n        scopal: 0.84\n        incompleteness: 0.82\n        lexical: 0.76\n        coreferential: 0.68\n      type_6way_f1: 0.48\n      layer_2way_f1: 0.58\n      gpu_hours: 3.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binary F1=0.82: ambiguity detection signal 存在。Per-type spread follows\n      surface marker salience: auth_scope (permission verbs, F1=0.88) easiest,\n      coref (discourse-level coreference, F1=0.68) hardest。6-way type F1=0.48\n      (above chance 0.17 但 practically weak) 和 layer 2-way F1=0.58 确认 type\n      boundaries surface-fuzzy——consistent with TOST equivalence。\n\n      Detection difficulty anti-correlates with risk: easiest-to-detect types\n      (auth_scope 0.88, CP 0.85) are also the most dangerous on GPT models。\n      This is practical silver lining——priority targets are also easy to find。\n\n      在 worst tier narrative 下, classifier 支持 practical message: binary\n      detection feasible (F1=0.82) and sufficient (type detection F1=0.48 too\n      weak to be useful, consistent with types being functionally equivalent)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: Classifier Performance\"\n        content: |\n          | Task                    | F1   | Precision | Recall |\n          |-------------------------|------|-----------|--------|\n          | Binary (amb vs unamb)   | 0.82 | 0.84      | 0.80   |\n          | 6-way type              | 0.48 | 0.50      | 0.46   |\n          | 2-way layer             | 0.58 | 0.60      | 0.56   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual y-axis bar: per-type F1 (left) vs per-type Δpp (right), showing anti-correlation。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Classifier PoC role in worst tier: demonstrates binary detection feasible,\n      type detection not——aligning with reframed message。Practical pipeline =\n      binary flag → human review, 不需要 type-specific handling。P2 priority\n      合理——non-core but concrete practical grounding。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9dd9ee42-9f53-44aa-92a5-74909781e0f9","total_cost_usd":2.244886,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51682,"cache_read_input_tokens":164709,"output_tokens":73167,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51682,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":61295,"cache_read_input_tokens":47956,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15567,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15567},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":10169,"outputTokens":29,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.010313999999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":6,"outputTokens":73167,"cacheReadInp